WEBVTT

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:10.040
♪ Cello Sonata No. 3 in A Major, Op. 69
Ludwig van Beethoven

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:43.270
Kabe Souko…

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.720
If you want to blame something, blame yourself…

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.490
That talent of yours…

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:59.140
It's all for the sake of the silent night.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:17.750
Detective Conan   Full Score of Fear

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:24.970
I'm high school detective, Kudou Shinichi.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:29.810
While visiting an amusement park with my childhood friend and classmate, Mouri Ran…

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:33.980
I witnessed a man in black in the midst of a suspicious transaction.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.110
While caught up in watching the deal…

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.940
I failed to notice his other partner coming up from behind me.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:43.560
I was forced by those men to swallow poison.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.070
And when I came to…

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:48.080
My body had shrunk.

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:50.950
If those guys found out that Kudou Shinichi was still alive…

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:52.640
They'd try to kill me again…

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.330
And the people around me would be at risk.

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:58.250
At Professor Agasa's suggestion, I decided to conceal my true identity.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.610
When Ran asked for my name, in that instant…

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:02.010
I became Edogawa Conan.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:04.220
In order to obtain information about those guys…

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:07.050
I went to live with Ran, whose father is a private detective.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:10.430
Let's go, Mitsuhiko!

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.270
Please leave it to me!

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:17.350
All right!

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:19.520
Mitsuhiko!

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:20.770
Conan-kun!

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:21.740
Huh?

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:23.610
Get it, Ayumi-chan!

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:25.670
Me?

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:31.580
Leave it to me!

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:39.960
Hooray!

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.690
These guys are my classmates now…

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:46.640
Genta…

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:47.510
Genta…  Ayumi…

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:48.180
Genta…  Ayumi…  and Mitsuhiko.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:50.810
They formed the Detective Boys…

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:52.860
And forced me to join.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.480
There's one other member.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.630
She is Haibara Ai.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:04:59.650
Real name:  Miyano Shiho.

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:06.570
Her parents, who passed away when she was a child, were scientists with the Black Organization.

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:09.830
Under the codename Sherry, she worked for them…

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:11.540
And developed that drug…

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:14.210
Apotoxin 4869.

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:25.340
However, her only sister, Miyano Akemi, was killed by those guys for resisting the Organization.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:30.180
In order to end her own life, she took the drug…

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.010
And her body shrunk.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.030
That's how she encountered us.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:39.650
We are both living the lives of first year elementary school students…

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.270
Until I reveal those guys' true identities.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:48.940
However, this tiny detective keeps forgetting his own situation.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:50.660
In conjunction with his superb deduction skills…

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:56.540
Using inventions created by Professor Agasa, he has solved many cases one after another.

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:02.210
Thanks to him, I'm always having shivers run down my spine.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:05.130
Well, it's music class now…

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:08.000
And he's sending shivers down my spine for a different reason.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:16.990
Look, it's the usual people.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.770
Even though I've gotten smaller, my mind remains the same…

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:25.200
The unbeaten great detective…

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:28.360
There's always one truth!

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:32.330
Doumoto Kazuki?

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:33.930
You've heard of him, haven't you, Shinichi?

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:34.450
Yeah.

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:38.730
Isn't he the founder of that music academy where that bombing occurred last week?

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:41.210
Actually…

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:44.000
I'm at that very place right now.

00:06:44.390 --> 00:06:47.360
Doumoto-san was a renowned pianist.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.870
But, unexpectedly, he switched to the organ.

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:53.160
And so, not only did they build a new concert hall…

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:56.940
They're bringing over a pipe organ from an old church in Germany.

00:06:58.220 --> 00:07:01.060
You mean the one that Bach himself played?

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:06.840
We're going to be able to attend the opening concert of Doumoto Hall.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:10.020
Furthermore, we even get to watch the rehearsal!

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:11.200
All thanks to Sonoko.

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:15.500
Oh yeah, Doumoto Hall was built by Suzuki Construction, wasn't it?

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.580
A piano key?

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:27.050
Did it fly all the way over here?

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:29.620
Say, why don't you come with, Shinichi?

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:32.380
You'll get to hear a Stradivarius played live.

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:38.130
Didn't you say you would like to hear one for yourself someday, since you play violin?

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:44.540
What's that person doing?

00:07:57.480 --> 00:07:59.850
Hey, are you listening, Shinichi?

00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:01.760
Oh, sorry, sorry.

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:04.080
Unfortunately, I'm in the middle of a case at the moment, so I'm a little busy.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:06.480
Can't you take even a little time off?

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:08.480
The rehearsal is the day after tomorrow.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:10.180
Sorry to disappoint you, but I'll have to pass.

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:12.240
The concert is next week on Tuesday.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:13.320
I really can't go.

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:15.180
Like I said, I'm working on a case—

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.900
But, you might be done with it by then.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:19.910
I already asked Sonoko to reserve a seat for—

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:23.150
Didn't I just say I couldn't? Don't go meddling in my affairs.

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:23.440
Damn.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:26.610
I'm meddling?

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:28.400
Ah, no—

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:30.730
Ah! I see how it is!

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:34.860
I guess I'm just some meddlesome karate idiot.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:37.070
You don't have to go that far…

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:38.630
Whatever.

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:43.250
Even if you listened to a Stradivarius, you'd never be anything like Holmes.

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:44.410
What?

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.180
Because, Shinichi…

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:47.630
You're tone-deaf!

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:50.090
Ran, you…

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:54.130
Well, keep on doing your best, Mr. Tone-Deaf Detective!

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:55.770
Jeez…

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:57.370
That deduction geek!

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:59.030
I'll never invite him again!

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:01.910
Jeez…

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:10.410
Hello?

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:11.650
Conan-kun?

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:13.780
What would you like for dinner tonight?

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:15.030
Uhm…

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:17.570
How about curry? Or is there something else…

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.030
Ah, no. Curry is fine.

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:21.480
That's good.

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:24.410
I'm really glad you're so agreeable, Conan-kun.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:29.130
Well, be careful and come home before it gets dark, all right?

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:30.520
Yes!

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:31.140
See you!

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:39.300
So when I'm Conan, I'm ''agreeable'', huh?

00:09:51.190 --> 00:10:00.520
♪ Toccata and Fugue in D Minor, BWV 565
Johann Sebastian Bach

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:27.560
Doumoto Kazuki     Organist & Composer

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:53.140
Wonderful! Very well played!

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:55.300
That was excellent, Doumoto-san.

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:57.820
That had a different sort of charisma, as compared to the piano.

00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:05.500
Wow, just like you'd expect from Doumoto Kazuki. That was magnificent indeed.

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:07.750
I've seen that person on TV before.

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:10.500
There, the man with the glasses.

00:12:11.050 --> 00:12:13.420
Ah! That's Fuwa Takumi-san.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:17.590
Fuwa Takumi     Doumoto Hall Director

00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:17.880
He has been Doumoto-san's sole piano tuner for the last 35 years.

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:21.260
He's now the director of Doumoto Hall.

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:23.590
That person…

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:27.670
The one who just turned around is a German, Hans Müller-san.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:29.760
He's a pipe organ tuner.

00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:33.940
Hans Müller     Organ Tuner

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.590
He seems to be at ease now, but…

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:34.950
He's had frequent disputes with Doumoto-san in the past.

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:39.530
And, the one interpreting next to him is Doumoto-san's son…

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:42.530
Doumoto Genya     Pianist & Doumoto Kazuki's Son

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:40.950
A pianist, Genya-san.

00:12:41.590 --> 00:12:43.540
He's the organizer for the upcoming performance.

00:12:44.690 --> 00:12:47.280
After that, we have those two ladies over there.

00:12:48.380 --> 00:12:50.540
Both of them are Doumoto-san's pupils…

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:54.490
The lady on the right is from Doumoto Academy's 9th class…

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.920
Chigusa Rara     Soprano

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:56.460
A soprano, Chigusa Rara-san.

00:12:58.180 --> 00:13:02.050
The nervous-looking person next to her is from the same academy, from its 8th class…

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:04.510
Yamane Shion     Violinist

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:04.180
A violinist, Yamane Shion-san.

00:13:05.420 --> 00:13:09.890
Oh, she's substituting for the person who was injured in the bombing incident, Kabe Souko-san, then?

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:11.080
Right, right.

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:16.270
Kabe-san's Stradivarius just so happened to be away for adjustments at the time of the incident, so it wasn't damaged.

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:19.190
Shion-san is just borrowing it for the performance.

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:23.110
And, the person sitting in the very first row is…

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:24.150
Akiba Reiko-san, right?

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:25.640
The soprano.

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:28.110
I figured you would know her.

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:30.630
She is pretty famous, after all.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:33.120
Akiba Reiko     Soprano

00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:35.750
All right, Shion, get ready.

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:37.040
Yes, sir.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:39.370
We will start from the first piece, Ave Maria.

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:39.910
Yes, sir.

00:13:48.190 --> 00:13:51.850
Judging from that, it seems you aren't ready to rehearse it with me yet, are you?

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:54.950
Oh, sorry, wait just one moment please.

00:13:56.150 --> 00:13:57.230
My apologies.

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:03.130
We finally get to hear a Stradivarius in person, Satou-san!

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:06.490
If it were up to me, I'd prefer an Amati.

00:14:07.670 --> 00:14:08.560
Be quiet!

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:29.250
♪ Ave Maria
Charles-Francois Gounod

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:48.910
That won't do, that won't do!

00:14:49.810 --> 00:14:51.040
That's completely unacceptable!

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.280
What have you been doing for this past week?

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:55.620
My apologies.

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:58.390
Was there something wrong with it?

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:01.420
No, I thought it sounded perfect.

00:15:02.030 --> 00:15:02.750
No…

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:05.880
For a Stradivarius, the sound isn't projecting properly…

00:15:06.270 --> 00:15:07.730
One more time, from the top.

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:08.500
Yes, sir!

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:34.750
What?

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:35.860
What happened?

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:37.740
It looks like one of the violin strings snapped.

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:39.420
My apologies!

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:40.600
I'll go replace it immediately!

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:44.290
How is the sound balance with the organ?

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:46.700
Hmm, there's no problem.

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:47.620
My, my…

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:50.470
I wonder if I'll even get to sing today.

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:55.020
Akiba-san, a moment of your time?

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:57.640
Will you at least let me visit the powder room?

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:06.230
Mouri-kun…

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:09.900
Do you have any leads on the culprit behind the bombing?

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:11.620
No, not yet.

00:16:12.210 --> 00:16:15.240
Plastic explosives were used though, right?

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:15.840
Yeah.

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:17.670
We also found a timer.

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:20.950
It was set to the time of the two victims' performance.

00:16:22.060 --> 00:16:23.830
Then, wouldn't that mean…

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:25.580
Sorry, Mouri-kun.

00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:30.010
I can't discuss details pertaining to the investigation here and now.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:32.170
Especially with children around…

00:16:33.390 --> 00:16:34.010
Children?

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:40.980
Go play with the other children!

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:41.930
Yeah, yeah…

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:45.400
It's so huge!

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:48.600
It's not just big, but beautiful as well.

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:49.560
It's amazing, isn't it?

00:16:50.060 --> 00:16:53.280
Hey, how do pipe organs make sound?

00:16:53.890 --> 00:16:58.640
The principle behind the sound production here is the same as with the recorders you play at school.

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:02.000
Look, there are a lot of pipes lined up together, aren't there?

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:08.000
Just like when you blow into a recorder, sound is produced when air passes through each of these pipes.

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:09.210
Air?

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:10.100
Really?

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:13.760
But there aren't any holes on those pipes like on a recorder!

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:15.210
Right.

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:19.450
For a recorder, you cover the holes with your fingers in order to produce notes of different pitches.

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:20.470
But, for a pipe organ…

00:17:23.470 --> 00:17:27.310
You press keys. Then, sound comes out of the pipe corresponding to the key you pressed.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:31.650
Each pipe produces its own unique sound.

00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:35.490
What are those switch-like things?

00:17:36.190 --> 00:17:37.190
Oh, these?

00:17:37.190 --> 00:17:39.600
These are known as “stops”.

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:43.500
When you pull these out, each one causes a different tone to be produced.

00:17:43.970 --> 00:17:46.090
For instance, if I pull this one out…

00:17:49.490 --> 00:17:50.460
That's a trumpet!

00:17:56.190 --> 00:17:57.090
A flute!

00:17:58.080 --> 00:18:02.720
Organists use a combination of all these sounds to add variety to their performance.

00:18:03.050 --> 00:18:04.120
I see!

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:05.450
We learned something new today!

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:07.140
And now, once again it's…

00:18:07.550 --> 00:18:09.520
Time for the long-awaited quiz!

00:18:10.180 --> 00:18:11.360
No one's been waiting…

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:16.180
A certain opera singer had a sore throat and was awaiting an operation.

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:20.990
However, they decided against the operation and got better after taking a pill they got from an old man.

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:24.950
And now, from the following options, who was the singer?

00:18:25.610 --> 00:18:26.910
1. Soprano.

00:18:27.550 --> 00:18:28.870
2. Alto.

00:18:29.390 --> 00:18:30.830
3. Tenor.

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:32.400
4. Bass.

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:39.830
This one's difficult…

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:41.930
Professor, how about a hint?

00:18:42.380 --> 00:18:44.720
How do you say “operation” in English?

00:18:45.280 --> 00:18:46.210
Operation.

00:18:46.670 --> 00:18:47.830
We usually just say ''ope''.

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:51.810
And also, it's an old man's pill, right?

00:18:52.890 --> 00:18:54.230
Conan-kun, you already know?

00:18:54.770 --> 00:18:55.540
Yeah.

00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:56.550
It's easy.

00:18:57.240 --> 00:18:57.780
First of all…

00:18:57.780 --> 00:18:58.560
Number one.

00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:04.010
The answer is number one: Soprano.

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:06.870
An opera singer gave up on an operation…

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:09.310
So you take away “ope” from “opera”, leaving “ra”.

00:19:10.510 --> 00:19:13.640
A “pill” is some medicine that's small and round.

00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:16.810
Thus, the ''old man's pill'' means using a small circle with the word “sofu” (grandfather).

00:19:17.660 --> 00:19:19.820
When you combine that with the “ra” from before…

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:21.230
Ra…

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:22.580
''Sofu'' with…

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:24.280
A small circle…

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:28.140
Soprano!

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:30.310
How stupid.

00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:34.810
You're right, but you didn't have to say it was stupid…

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:38.120
Excuse me, Akiba-san.

00:19:38.560 --> 00:19:39.740
We've been waiting to talk…

00:19:40.270 --> 00:19:41.390
Sheesh.

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:42.770
This had better be over quickly.

00:19:45.970 --> 00:19:52.500
We would like to ask you one more time about the e-mail Kabe Souko-san sent you just before the explosion.

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:57.500
“It's impossible to work with a bunch of amateurs who can't differentiate between sounds.”

00:19:58.160 --> 00:19:59.840
What is the meaning of this e-mail?

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:01.070
The meaning?

00:20:01.420 --> 00:20:02.800
It's just like it says.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:06.860
I've mentioned it before, Kabe-san and I are…

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:10.140
You met her for the first time during the press conference for this public concert, right?

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:11.210
Yeah.

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:15.520
At that time, she said she would listen to the performances of those two who passed away…

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:17.750
And would e-mail me her thoughts.

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:21.420
In other words, based on the difference between those two people's style and Kabe-san's style…

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:25.460
As a musician, her remark that they couldn't tell the difference between sounds…

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:27.930
Meant they couldn't perform together, isn't that right?

00:20:28.840 --> 00:20:29.990
Something like that, I suppose.

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:32.010
Why don't you ask her directly?

00:20:32.470 --> 00:20:33.660
Hasn't she regained consciousness yet?

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:36.170
Yes, she is awake, but…

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:37.910
Due to the shock of the explosion…

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:40.050
She's lost her memory of the incident.

00:20:41.220 --> 00:20:42.010
Is that so?

00:20:43.980 --> 00:20:45.090
There's one more thing.

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:48.350
This item was found at the crime scene.

00:20:49.660 --> 00:20:50.930
The body joint of a flute!

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:52.030
That's right.

00:20:52.450 --> 00:20:58.400
The head joint, the body joint, and the foot joint. A flute can be separated into those three sections.

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:01.880
Could it be that some student left it behind?

00:21:02.180 --> 00:21:05.890
That's possible, but only the body joint being there makes it strange.

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:09.730
Does anything come to mind?

00:21:11.050 --> 00:21:11.860
Akiba-san?

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:14.620
No, nothing.

00:21:15.090 --> 00:21:16.290
I've had enough.

00:21:17.550 --> 00:21:18.880
Wait, Akiba-san!

00:21:30.270 --> 00:21:31.390
What's that?

00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:33.560
What's that you're drinking?

00:21:34.050 --> 00:21:34.700
Tea.

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:36.640
Let us have some too!

00:21:36.950 --> 00:21:37.650
Nope.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:38.440
Stingy.

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:42.440
Could it be that there are ingredients 
in it that are good for the throat?

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:43.600
Nothing like that.

00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:48.160
If that were really true, we might be able to get first in the chorus competition if we drank it!

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:49.990
Chorus competition?

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:50.490
Yeah!

00:21:50.940 --> 00:21:53.850
There's an inter-class chorus competition coming up.

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:55.170
I know!

00:21:55.170 --> 00:21:57.290
Why don't you coach us for the competition?

00:21:59.090 --> 00:22:03.870
We'll be practicing in our school's music classroom the day after tomorrow starting at 2:00 P.M.

00:22:03.870 --> 00:22:06.640
Even though Ran-oneesan will be playing the piano for us…

00:22:07.330 --> 00:22:10.270
The person showing us how to sing is the problem.

00:22:10.270 --> 00:22:11.440
Hey, you brats!

00:22:13.030 --> 00:22:14.850
Who did you say was a problem?

00:22:18.710 --> 00:22:19.830
Jeez!

00:22:19.830 --> 00:22:22.110
I'm sorry. Please don't mind them.

00:22:23.500 --> 00:22:25.780
I hope the song isn't the 9th (daiku).

00:22:26.400 --> 00:22:28.070
I don't like that one.

00:22:28.600 --> 00:22:30.470
It isn't the Carpenter's (daiku) Song!

00:22:30.470 --> 00:22:32.160
It's Teitan Elementary's school song!

00:22:33.430 --> 00:22:38.010
When she said “9th” (daiku), she meant Beethoven's 9th Symphony.

00:22:38.620 --> 00:22:39.080
Is that true?

00:22:40.730 --> 00:22:41.760
Fine.

00:22:41.760 --> 00:22:43.120
I'll be your chorus coach.

00:22:43.870 --> 00:22:45.920
Think of it as a favor from a Teitan Elementary alumnus.

00:22:47.020 --> 00:22:48.090
Is that so?

00:22:48.730 --> 00:22:50.990
Therefore, please go home now.

00:22:50.990 --> 00:22:52.090
And stay out of the way.

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:53.550
Yes…

00:22:56.460 --> 00:23:00.080
Although I'm glad to have her be our chorus coach…

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:02.170
That old lady is kind of rude…

00:23:02.750 --> 00:23:03.520
A bit.

00:23:04.490 --> 00:23:07.250
She seems to give off the stereotypical celebrity aura…

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:08.580
Yeah.

00:23:08.580 --> 00:23:10.200
She's a little like you, Haibara.

00:23:13.210 --> 00:23:16.410
No, I mean, she's really pretty…

00:23:16.670 --> 00:23:20.460
I can't tell whether Akiba-san is actually ill-tempered or kind.

00:23:20.650 --> 00:23:22.580
Yeah. But perhaps…

00:23:23.390 --> 00:23:27.920
Maybe she chased everyone out because she was being considerate of Shion-san, who was so nervous.

00:23:28.630 --> 00:23:30.260
Aren't you reading too much into it?

00:23:30.260 --> 00:23:31.080
You think so?

00:24:00.690 --> 00:24:02.260
Love - 30.

00:24:02.260 --> 00:24:06.320
Jeez, getting all serious against an impromptu opponent.

00:24:09.490 --> 00:24:12.720
A lion goes all out even when chasing a rabbit.

00:24:13.050 --> 00:24:14.190
Yes, yes…

00:24:14.190 --> 00:24:16.080
I guess I'm the ''rabbit'' then.

00:24:16.550 --> 00:24:18.970
Oh yeah, let's do mixed doubles next time.

00:24:19.370 --> 00:24:21.060
We can call Makoto-san and Shinichi-kun.

00:24:24.760 --> 00:24:25.520
Shinichi?

00:24:26.930 --> 00:24:28.980
That deduction geek…

00:24:46.200 --> 00:24:47.090
No way…

00:24:51.250 --> 00:24:53.760
I see, so you're having a fight with Shinichi-kun.

00:24:54.540 --> 00:24:56.710
I can't do anything about a matrimonial quarrel, you know.

00:24:56.710 --> 00:24:57.720
It's nothing like that!

00:24:58.530 --> 00:25:00.710
But you two are always like that…

00:25:00.710 --> 00:25:03.170
You always make up right away afterward.

00:25:05.100 --> 00:25:06.760
But it lasted a long time back then…

00:25:07.570 --> 00:25:09.890
You didn't talk to each other for about a week, right?

00:25:10.620 --> 00:25:11.400
When was that?

00:25:11.870 --> 00:25:13.860
Remember, when we just turned twelve…

00:25:14.490 --> 00:25:16.320
Ah, I remember!

00:25:16.320 --> 00:25:17.090
That's the time…

00:25:17.690 --> 00:25:19.830
Wait, what were we fighting about?

00:25:20.210 --> 00:25:22.220
Then, how did the both of you make up?

00:25:24.680 --> 00:25:26.070
You forgot everything?

00:25:27.070 --> 00:25:28.080
I think it was…

00:25:34.400 --> 00:25:35.830
Stop, stop. Hold it right there.

00:25:36.990 --> 00:25:39.390
Why did you two go home together when you were fighting?

00:25:40.850 --> 00:25:42.850
Because our houses were in the same direction.

00:25:45.990 --> 00:25:46.760
I give up.

00:25:46.760 --> 00:25:47.310
Continue.

00:25:55.290 --> 00:25:57.030
At that time, someone was singing…

00:25:58.080 --> 00:26:00.860
At that time, we heard someone singing by the river bank.

00:26:01.380 --> 00:26:04.290
And, as we listened, somehow we just…

00:26:04.830 --> 00:26:06.420
You made up!

00:26:06.900 --> 00:26:08.210
And? What song was it?

00:26:09.450 --> 00:26:10.570
What was it?

00:26:11.800 --> 00:26:15.280
Huh? I think it was a famous song, but…

00:26:15.560 --> 00:26:16.130
Hey, hey…

00:26:16.830 --> 00:26:19.220
But, how should I put it…

00:26:19.220 --> 00:26:21.700
It was a song that reached into my heart.

00:26:25.360 --> 00:26:29.050
On this hill of ardent green

00:26:25.360 --> 00:26:29.050
Midori moyuru oka

00:26:29.370 --> 00:26:33.100
With the distant mountain echo

00:26:29.370 --> 00:26:33.100
Tooku yama biko mo

00:26:33.480 --> 00:26:37.080
We sing with smiling faces

00:26:33.480 --> 00:26:37.080
Utatteru egao de

00:26:37.320 --> 00:26:41.030
The brilliant sunshine

00:26:37.320 --> 00:26:41.030
Mabushii taiyou

00:26:41.380 --> 00:26:44.940
Engraved on our hearts

00:26:41.380 --> 00:26:44.940
Kokoro no kizamou

00:26:45.360 --> 00:26:48.980
We seize the future

00:26:45.360 --> 00:26:48.980
Mirai wo tsukame

00:26:49.390 --> 00:26:57.080
Teitan  Teitan  Teitan Elementary

00:26:49.390 --> 00:26:57.080
Teitan  Teitan  Teitan shougakkou

00:26:57.280 --> 00:27:05.340
Teitan  Teitan  Teitan Elementary

00:26:57.280 --> 00:27:05.340
Teitan  Teitan  Teitan shougakkou

00:27:14.810 --> 00:27:15.940
How was it?

00:27:15.940 --> 00:27:17.140
The children's singing?

00:27:18.960 --> 00:27:19.780
Let's see…

00:27:21.600 --> 00:27:22.570
Firstly, you!

00:27:23.450 --> 00:27:24.880
Your voice is too loud.

00:27:24.880 --> 00:27:26.540
Try to blend in with the others!

00:27:28.090 --> 00:27:30.000
And the freckled boy next to him.

00:27:30.550 --> 00:27:34.540
Even though you're in tune, occasionally you're lacking in feeling.

00:27:35.410 --> 00:27:38.550
Could it be because you keep staring at the face of the girl in front of you?

00:27:39.020 --> 00:27:40.300
In front?

00:27:40.590 --> 00:27:42.010
Isn't it Haibara?

00:27:44.980 --> 00:27:46.470
And, this girl.

00:27:47.320 --> 00:27:48.350
You sing well…

00:27:49.100 --> 00:27:50.870
But you should sing more like a child.

00:27:51.220 --> 00:27:52.830
It's because I'm not a child.

00:27:53.130 --> 00:27:53.690
Hey, hey…

00:27:55.340 --> 00:27:58.960
Your pitch is accurate and you sing with expression, well done.

00:28:00.740 --> 00:28:03.600
As for you, don't be cramped by voices around you.

00:28:04.030 --> 00:28:05.980
Have more confidence.

00:28:04.640 --> 00:28:05.700
She's just like you'd expect.

00:28:06.390 --> 00:28:10.170
Even without listening properly, she can tell everyone's voices apart.

00:28:10.410 --> 00:28:11.450
Yeah.

00:28:11.450 --> 00:28:12.960
A musician's ears.

00:28:13.270 --> 00:28:14.200
The problem is…

00:28:14.940 --> 00:28:15.330
You!

00:28:16.950 --> 00:28:17.530
Yes?

00:28:17.800 --> 00:28:19.940
You were completely out of tune from beginning to end!

00:28:20.310 --> 00:28:21.550
You weren't doing it on purpose, were you?

00:28:22.540 --> 00:28:23.450
No.

00:28:23.450 --> 00:28:24.890
It wasn't on purpose!

00:28:24.890 --> 00:28:26.740
It's just that Conan-kun is tone-deaf!

00:28:26.920 --> 00:28:28.260
What sort of follow-up is that?

00:28:31.210 --> 00:28:33.680
Worst of all, the piano sounded weird too.

00:28:34.940 --> 00:28:37.000
The sound was flat the whole time.

00:28:37.690 --> 00:28:39.540
Hasn't it been tuned properly?

00:28:39.540 --> 00:28:40.470
Really?

00:28:40.820 --> 00:28:42.500
No way. I didn't notice anything.

00:28:43.520 --> 00:28:44.990
I thought so too.

00:28:45.630 --> 00:28:46.390
This person…

00:28:48.240 --> 00:28:49.020
Akiba-san…

00:28:49.400 --> 00:28:51.040
Do you have perfect pitch?

00:28:51.410 --> 00:28:52.870
Yeah, you could say that.

00:28:53.680 --> 00:28:55.650
What's that? ''Perfect pitch''?

00:28:56.060 --> 00:29:01.130
It's the ability to listen to a sound and be able to name the pitch and note immediately.

00:29:01.410 --> 00:29:02.230
For instance…

00:29:07.990 --> 00:29:09.330
E5 - Mi.

00:29:12.420 --> 00:29:14.920
B3 and F5's - Si and Fa.

00:29:14.920 --> 00:29:15.640
That's right!

00:29:15.910 --> 00:29:16.740
Amazing!

00:29:17.090 --> 00:29:18.980
That's why you are so good at singing!

00:29:19.450 --> 00:29:20.810
Well, I wonder…

00:29:21.390 --> 00:29:26.700
I don't know that perfect pitch is absolutely necessary for a musician, but still…

00:29:27.470 --> 00:29:29.860
It seems to be an inborn ability for me.

00:29:29.860 --> 00:29:32.040
I've heard you can achieve it through training as well.

00:29:32.690 --> 00:29:36.500
I believe that was likely the case with the former piano tuner, Fuwa-san.

00:29:36.860 --> 00:29:39.140
Well, that's all for me.

00:29:39.520 --> 00:29:41.150
For the rest, please practice on your own.

00:29:41.840 --> 00:29:43.850
If your singing gets better…

00:29:43.850 --> 00:29:44.820
I'll listen again.

00:29:45.770 --> 00:29:47.090
You're leaving already?

00:29:48.010 --> 00:29:50.410
We would like to hear a demonstration before you leave.

00:29:50.410 --> 00:29:51.260
Agreed!

00:29:53.160 --> 00:29:54.600
How much are you paying me?

00:29:57.060 --> 00:30:00.310
Professionals don't sing without being paid.

00:30:00.490 --> 00:30:01.030
See you.

00:30:01.840 --> 00:30:02.770
This is it, this is it…

00:30:04.600 --> 00:30:06.340
Hey! That's my tea!

00:30:06.690 --> 00:30:08.010
Thanks for the tea!

00:30:13.490 --> 00:30:14.310
What's wrong, Genta?

00:30:16.090 --> 00:30:17.000
What's going on?

00:30:17.000 --> 00:30:17.730
Genta-kun!

00:30:18.070 --> 00:30:18.960
Genta-kun!

00:30:19.700 --> 00:30:21.060
Are you all right, Genta-kun?

00:30:23.890 --> 00:30:26.790
Someone put something in there…

00:30:27.300 --> 00:30:28.260
That's what you're thinking, right?

00:30:28.770 --> 00:30:29.480
Impossible!

00:30:30.020 --> 00:30:30.910
How could this…

00:30:32.340 --> 00:30:34.000
At any rate, let's get him to the hospital.

00:30:36.390 --> 00:30:38.060
Will Genta-kun be all right?

00:30:38.520 --> 00:30:40.400
He seemed to be in a lot of pain, huh?

00:30:41.310 --> 00:30:42.610
His eyes were all red.

00:30:43.200 --> 00:30:45.360
When was the last time you drank any of that tea?

00:30:46.760 --> 00:30:48.110
Sometime before noon, I would think.

00:30:48.600 --> 00:30:49.240
Where?

00:30:49.840 --> 00:30:53.670
I borrowed a practice room at the Doumoto Academy…

00:30:53.670 --> 00:30:55.080
In order to practice my singing.

00:30:55.710 --> 00:30:57.140
Before leaving, I went to the ladies' room.

00:30:57.620 --> 00:31:02.540
During that time, I left that bottle, along with the rest of my things, in the practice room.

00:31:03.180 --> 00:31:05.550
If someone had put something in it…

00:31:05.550 --> 00:31:06.520
It would have been then.

00:31:07.100 --> 00:31:08.550
But, who could it be?

00:31:09.870 --> 00:31:11.240
Thank you very much.

00:31:14.190 --> 00:31:14.980
Genta-kun!

00:31:16.220 --> 00:31:17.180
Are you all right?

00:31:17.570 --> 00:31:19.020
Not all right at all…

00:31:19.700 --> 00:31:21.090
What did the doctor say?

00:31:21.940 --> 00:31:23.730
His throat is quite inflamed, but…

00:31:24.220 --> 00:31:25.990
He'll recover in four or five days.

00:31:25.990 --> 00:31:27.260
You'll recover!

00:31:27.260 --> 00:31:27.900
Thank goodness!

00:31:28.360 --> 00:31:33.290
But, on the contrary, it means that he can't speak properly for the next four days.

00:31:33.290 --> 00:31:34.310
Yeah.

00:31:34.310 --> 00:31:36.870
There are three more days until the Doumoto Hall concert.

00:31:37.410 --> 00:31:38.780
If Reiko-san had drank from it…

00:31:39.190 --> 00:31:40.770
She might have been unable to perform.

00:31:43.170 --> 00:31:44.450
Tell Inspector Megure…

00:31:44.910 --> 00:31:47.190
To analyze the contents of that bottle.

00:31:47.720 --> 00:31:49.230
Then, I'll go report it.

00:31:50.040 --> 00:31:51.090
But, before that…

00:31:51.570 --> 00:31:53.680
As for Genta-kun, we'll get him home.

00:31:54.070 --> 00:31:54.830
Me too.

00:31:54.830 --> 00:31:55.640
I'll go too.

00:31:56.380 --> 00:31:58.390
I must meet this boy's parents and ask them…

00:31:59.210 --> 00:32:01.100
''How can he take someone else's drink without permission?''

00:32:01.100 --> 00:32:02.850
''What sort of upbringing did he have?''

00:32:03.420 --> 00:32:04.690
I'm sorry…

00:32:04.690 --> 00:32:05.920
Genta-kun…

00:32:14.860 --> 00:32:16.330
Cheer up, Genta-kun.

00:32:17.330 --> 00:32:18.520
Those four days…

00:32:18.520 --> 00:32:19.450
Will pass by in a flash.

00:32:20.980 --> 00:32:25.420
I also want… to take… the old man's pill.

00:32:26.200 --> 00:32:29.130
It's really the professor's quiz come true.

00:32:39.160 --> 00:32:40.810
Everyone, step to the side.

00:32:40.810 --> 00:32:41.490
No!

00:32:41.490 --> 00:32:42.150
Run!

00:32:44.390 --> 00:32:45.010
Hurry!

00:32:50.110 --> 00:32:51.530
Damn! I can't see their face!

00:32:55.020 --> 00:32:56.450
Now! Turn right!

00:33:18.570 --> 00:33:19.140
What!?

00:33:33.480 --> 00:33:34.280
Are you all right!?

00:33:41.870 --> 00:33:42.490
Shit!

00:33:45.800 --> 00:33:47.010
Are you all right?

00:33:47.010 --> 00:33:47.300
Yeah…

00:33:48.170 --> 00:33:49.870
What was with that truck?

00:33:49.870 --> 00:33:51.560
Going the wrong direction on a one-way street!

00:33:51.560 --> 00:33:52.450
Reiko-sensei!

00:33:52.990 --> 00:33:53.920
Your leg's bleeding…

00:33:55.620 --> 00:33:56.880
It's no big deal.

00:33:58.950 --> 00:34:01.740
Did the attack stop because of the taxi?

00:34:02.940 --> 00:34:04.100
Or was it…

00:34:04.420 --> 00:34:06.960
Well, sorry, but I'll leave these kids to you.

00:34:08.360 --> 00:34:10.170
I'm going home in this taxi.

00:34:10.700 --> 00:34:13.150
Tell the police about what just happened.

00:34:14.150 --> 00:34:15.190
You're leaving?

00:34:15.940 --> 00:34:18.860
Being with you is just bringing me bad luck.

00:34:19.460 --> 00:34:20.700
How could you…

00:34:20.700 --> 00:34:21.660
That's mean.

00:35:20.870 --> 00:35:21.420
Inspector!

00:35:22.540 --> 00:35:23.920
What about the cause of the explosion?

00:35:23.920 --> 00:35:24.730
Yes.

00:35:24.730 --> 00:35:29.480
We've determined that the room was filled by leaking propane gas, which was ignited by the lighting of a match.

00:35:29.480 --> 00:35:33.520
However, there's evidence that the gas detector had been deliberately broken.

00:35:34.060 --> 00:35:36.270
That means it wasn't an accident; it was murder.

00:35:36.660 --> 00:35:38.820
The deceased was the shop owner…

00:35:39.150 --> 00:35:41.370
Shida Osamu-san, aged 36.

00:35:41.370 --> 00:35:45.780
Shida-san was a violinist and was from Doumoto Academy's 1st class.

00:35:46.120 --> 00:35:47.310
The 1st class?

00:35:47.860 --> 00:35:50.710
It's the same as the two victims of the last bombing incident.

00:35:51.380 --> 00:35:53.370
I don't think that's just a coincidence.

00:35:53.370 --> 00:35:53.840
Yeah.

00:35:54.200 --> 00:35:55.000
It wasn't a coincidence.

00:35:55.810 --> 00:35:56.620
Detective Satou.

00:35:59.290 --> 00:36:00.420
We found this inside the shop.

00:36:01.490 --> 00:36:02.150
What's this?

00:36:02.830 --> 00:36:04.450
The foot joint of a flute.

00:36:05.340 --> 00:36:06.230
There's no doubt about it.

00:36:06.900 --> 00:36:08.750
This is a series of murders committed by the same culprit.

00:36:09.520 --> 00:36:12.600
Furthermore, the culprit has left us a message.

00:36:13.050 --> 00:36:14.830
The body joint and the foot joint, huh?

00:36:15.490 --> 00:36:17.540
There's still the head joint left.

00:36:19.120 --> 00:36:22.950
In that case, there will be another murder…

00:36:58.520 --> 00:37:03.820
The man who drowned after falling from his paraglider yesterday, Sone Hisao-san, right?

00:37:04.300 --> 00:37:05.060
Yeah.

00:37:05.060 --> 00:37:07.370
He seems to have been a viola player…

00:37:07.960 --> 00:37:11.290
The thing is, we've found out that he was a student in Doumoto Academy's 1st class.

00:37:12.230 --> 00:37:13.460
In that case, could it be…

00:37:13.460 --> 00:37:14.250
Yeah.

00:37:14.760 --> 00:37:17.550
He was a classmate of the victims from last week, Mizumi-san and Renjou-san…

00:37:18.010 --> 00:37:21.540
Along with Shida-san, who died in an explosion two days ago.

00:37:22.420 --> 00:37:26.720
Furthermore, until two years ago, the four of them were members of a piano quartet.

00:37:29.230 --> 00:37:32.380
As I thought, it was a series of murders by the same culprit.

00:37:32.380 --> 00:37:33.620
There's no doubt about it.

00:37:34.280 --> 00:37:37.070
According to what the prefectural police said, the cloth wings…

00:37:37.560 --> 00:37:41.780
And the canopy showed traces of minute cuts from a bladed object.

00:37:41.780 --> 00:37:45.570
And on top of that, under the seat in Sone-san's car…

00:37:46.170 --> 00:37:49.950
You found the remaining section of the flute, the head joint, right?

00:37:50.860 --> 00:37:51.740
Y-Yeah…

00:37:52.380 --> 00:37:55.880
But if all the flute parts have been assembled…

00:37:55.880 --> 00:37:58.880
Doesn't that mean this is the end of the serial murders?

00:37:59.190 --> 00:38:00.690
I would hope so.

00:38:01.250 --> 00:38:02.250
Oh yeah, Ran-kun.

00:38:02.250 --> 00:38:02.800
Yes?

00:38:03.430 --> 00:38:06.990
In the thermos that you left with us…

00:38:07.570 --> 00:38:09.490
The forensics examination found that…

00:38:09.490 --> 00:38:12.240
Chemicals of a highly irritative nature were present.

00:38:13.240 --> 00:38:15.430
It's too serious to be passed off as a prank.

00:38:16.100 --> 00:38:17.890
And the truck that attacked us?

00:38:18.340 --> 00:38:21.110
It had been stolen somewhere near the scene.

00:38:21.820 --> 00:38:24.630
In other words, since placing a drug in the thermos…

00:38:24.630 --> 00:38:27.070
Failed to hurt Akiba-san…

00:38:27.760 --> 00:38:30.860
They went to their next plan and stole a truck to run her over…

00:38:31.360 --> 00:38:33.790
All to achieve their original objective.

00:38:34.610 --> 00:38:41.630
That objective being, to render Akiba-san unable to perform at Doumoto Hall's opening.

00:38:43.300 --> 00:38:46.510
Say, if Reiko-san couldn't appear for the public performance…

00:38:46.510 --> 00:38:47.970
Who would replace her?

00:38:48.560 --> 00:38:51.340
Most likely Chigusa Rara, I'd imagine.

00:38:52.720 --> 00:38:55.030
Initially, she was the first choice for the soprano part.

00:38:55.430 --> 00:39:00.390
She's a member of Doumoto Academy's 9th class, and also Doumoto-shi's pupil.

00:39:02.250 --> 00:39:03.200
But at this point…

00:39:03.560 --> 00:39:06.660
The already confirmed performer, Kabe Souko-san…

00:39:07.110 --> 00:39:12.110
Recommended Akiba-san, with whom she had desired to perform, for the part.

00:39:12.880 --> 00:39:15.240
And that's how they decided on her.

00:39:15.850 --> 00:39:18.240
And so, the next question would be…

00:39:18.240 --> 00:39:20.370
How do these four factor into the case?

00:39:20.950 --> 00:39:21.840
As of now…

00:39:22.300 --> 00:39:25.210
We haven't found any connection between Akiba-san and the four others.

00:39:25.830 --> 00:39:27.100
All that we know is…

00:39:27.100 --> 00:39:30.620
The connection between Kabe-san and the first two bombing victims.

00:39:31.510 --> 00:39:33.510
But there's still the issue of the performance…

00:39:34.160 --> 00:39:38.810
The bomb was planted under the floorboard near the two victims.

00:39:39.270 --> 00:39:40.240
If that's the case…

00:39:40.820 --> 00:39:44.150
Kabe-san was simply unfortunate to be involved?

00:39:44.430 --> 00:39:47.280
It's too early to decide that.

00:39:47.280 --> 00:39:50.530
There are others with motives to kill Kabe-san.

00:39:51.420 --> 00:39:54.950
You mean the candidate before Akiba-san, Chigusa Rara?

00:39:55.560 --> 00:39:56.600
There's one more.

00:39:57.140 --> 00:40:00.660
Kabe-san's replacement, Yamane Shion.

00:40:03.660 --> 00:40:04.580
Her too?

00:40:04.980 --> 00:40:05.640
Yeah.

00:40:06.100 --> 00:40:08.480
If, after borrowing the Stradivarius from Kabe-san…

00:40:08.990 --> 00:40:12.660
She were to perform at this concert, which is attended by internationally renowned musicians…

00:40:13.010 --> 00:40:14.790
And give an outstanding performance…

00:40:15.290 --> 00:40:18.850
She could become world famous overnight.

00:40:20.480 --> 00:40:22.220
However, there's one more possibility.

00:40:22.800 --> 00:40:25.190
She was one of Doumoto-shi's prized students.

00:40:26.050 --> 00:40:28.930
The truth is, the reason that Kabe-san was selected for the performance…

00:40:29.440 --> 00:40:33.960
Wasn't that he wanted her, but rather he had his eye on her Stradivarius.

00:40:34.600 --> 00:40:37.890
He had always intended for Shion-san to perform.

00:40:38.360 --> 00:40:41.570
And so, he designated her as the stand-in at the onset.

00:40:42.260 --> 00:40:46.670
Then, he ensured that Kabe-san was seriously injured in order to get his hands on the Stradivarius.

00:40:47.060 --> 00:40:49.210
This possibility cannot be dismissed either.

00:40:50.530 --> 00:40:54.140
Human relationships are so complicated; it's becoming even harder to understand.

00:40:54.520 --> 00:40:55.220
In short…

00:40:55.680 --> 00:41:00.330
The person who has a motive against both Kabe-san and Reiko-san is Chigusa Rara-san, right?

00:41:01.180 --> 00:41:05.130
Those who have a motive only against Kabe-san are Doumoto-san and Shion-san.

00:41:05.700 --> 00:41:10.000
But we still haven't discovered what motives these three may have had for killing the other four.

00:41:11.230 --> 00:41:12.400
Is that right?

00:41:13.040 --> 00:41:14.570
Yeah, that's right.

00:41:16.510 --> 00:41:20.230
Oh yeah, the piano in the practice room where the explosion occurred…

00:41:20.610 --> 00:41:23.000
Could there be anything special about it?

00:41:23.440 --> 00:41:26.900
No, I haven't heard that there's anything special, but…

00:41:27.360 --> 00:41:28.790
Why do you think that?

00:41:29.130 --> 00:41:31.050
When I went there the other day…

00:41:31.050 --> 00:41:35.400
I saw Fuwa-san holding onto a fragment of a piano key, as though it were really precious.

00:41:35.910 --> 00:41:38.600
So I thought there might be something special about it…

00:41:38.600 --> 00:41:39.740
Hey!

00:41:39.740 --> 00:41:41.940
Don't go wandering around on your own!

00:41:42.430 --> 00:41:43.470
Sorry…

00:41:44.010 --> 00:41:49.270
That piano was the one Doumoto-shi played in his home for more than 30 years, wasn't it?

00:41:50.080 --> 00:41:52.210
When he retired from being a pianist…

00:41:52.680 --> 00:41:56.280
He decided to move it to the academy so that the younger musicians could practice on it.

00:41:57.120 --> 00:41:59.530
Of course, when the piano was in Doumoto-shi's home…

00:41:59.530 --> 00:42:01.390
And even after it was moved to the academy…

00:42:01.390 --> 00:42:03.700
It was always tuned by Fuwa-shi.

00:42:05.300 --> 00:42:09.290
Well, perhaps to him, the piano was just like a son.

00:42:09.790 --> 00:42:11.070
Got that, brat?

00:42:12.440 --> 00:42:13.890
Come to think of it…

00:42:13.890 --> 00:42:17.060
Fuwa-san was criticizing those four before…

00:42:17.680 --> 00:42:20.770
He said their problem was their shallow approach to life or something.

00:42:20.770 --> 00:42:25.080
But there's no way he'd kill the four of them over that, would he?

00:42:25.700 --> 00:42:26.730
I guess not.

00:42:27.200 --> 00:42:33.280
If, for the sake of argument, you assume he wanted to kill them because he couldn't stand their approach to life or whatever…

00:42:33.670 --> 00:42:37.230
That still doesn't connect to what just happened with Akiba-san.

00:42:38.380 --> 00:42:39.580
Inspector-dono…

00:42:39.580 --> 00:42:44.090
Wouldn't it be best to consider Akiba-san's case separate from the other four?

00:42:44.500 --> 00:42:49.310
But, all these cases so far have been centered around Doumoto-shi…

00:42:49.310 --> 00:42:52.220
I don't think that can all be a mere coincidence.

00:42:52.820 --> 00:42:54.060
I suppose…

00:42:54.390 --> 00:42:55.340
Still, at any rate…

00:42:55.940 --> 00:42:58.950
At the very least, before the end of the concert in two days…

00:42:59.300 --> 00:43:02.360
We have to consider whether to guard Akiba-san.

00:43:02.980 --> 00:43:05.100
I already sent Takagi-kun, but…

00:43:05.450 --> 00:43:06.270
Um…

00:43:06.270 --> 00:43:09.560
She turned me away, saying I was annoying…

00:43:10.740 --> 00:43:11.490
Jeez…

00:43:11.490 --> 00:43:13.610
What the hell were you thinking, Takagi?

00:43:13.610 --> 00:43:15.970
If Reiko-san is attacked again…

00:43:15.970 --> 00:43:17.650
Not even a written apology will help anything.

00:43:17.650 --> 00:43:21.960
Ah, but she said she would be staying home today and tomorrow…

00:43:21.960 --> 00:43:23.250
You idiot!

00:43:23.250 --> 00:43:25.310
Is there anyone who would just say ''Oh, I see,'' and leave!?

00:43:25.560 --> 00:43:26.450
I'm sorry!

00:43:29.530 --> 00:43:30.610
I'm leaving!

00:43:32.890 --> 00:43:34.090
Conan-kun!

00:43:34.790 --> 00:43:36.180
Morning, Conan-kun!

00:43:36.760 --> 00:43:37.880
Good morning!

00:43:38.630 --> 00:43:39.630
What's with you guys?

00:43:40.020 --> 00:43:41.150
So early in the morning.

00:43:41.500 --> 00:43:43.470
We're going to see Kamen Yaiba!

00:43:43.940 --> 00:43:44.930
Kamen Yaiba?

00:43:45.140 --> 00:43:49.460
They'll be filming in Ryokuchi Park today, by the Teimuzu River…

00:43:49.460 --> 00:43:51.010
According to the top secret information I got!

00:43:51.340 --> 00:43:54.720
We think that Genta-kun will recover after seeing that.

00:43:55.770 --> 00:43:58.230
I can't see how that would make him better…

00:43:58.670 --> 00:44:01.380
So we came to invite you, Conan-kun, but…

00:44:01.380 --> 00:44:02.580
Are you going somewhere?

00:44:03.120 --> 00:44:04.320
Yeah, sort of.

00:44:04.710 --> 00:44:05.600
Sort of?

00:44:06.260 --> 00:44:07.790
It's nothing big.

00:44:07.910 --> 00:44:10.620
Could it be more important than your friendship with Genta-kun?

00:44:12.220 --> 00:44:13.530
I guess I have no choice.

00:44:14.190 --> 00:44:15.420
I'm going to Reiko-san's.

00:44:15.910 --> 00:44:16.840
Reiko-sensei?

00:44:17.190 --> 00:44:18.580
You'd better not!

00:44:18.970 --> 00:44:21.330
She'll get mad again.

00:44:21.330 --> 00:44:25.260
Yeah, I guess, but if I don't protect her from the bad guys…

00:44:25.660 --> 00:44:27.860
By ''bad guys,'' you mean from that time?

00:44:28.170 --> 00:44:29.930
Why do you have to protect her?

00:44:31.380 --> 00:44:32.950
Yeah, I wonder why that is…

00:44:33.690 --> 00:44:35.550
I don't really know myself, but…

00:44:36.210 --> 00:44:39.900
Somehow I feel that I can't live with myself if I don't.

00:44:48.800 --> 00:44:51.280
He must mean that he's in love…

00:44:51.660 --> 00:44:53.710
Conan-kun prefers older women.

00:44:54.250 --> 00:44:55.700
How can that be?

00:44:56.320 --> 00:44:58.750
Anyway, I'll leave Genta to the two of you.

00:44:59.220 --> 00:44:59.670
I'm relying on you.

00:45:00.070 --> 00:45:00.960
Conan-kun!

00:45:02.460 --> 00:45:05.240
Does that mean that he trusts us?

00:45:06.010 --> 00:45:06.780
Probably.

00:45:40.970 --> 00:45:41.640
Yes?

00:45:44.370 --> 00:45:45.840
Good morning, Reiko-san!

00:45:46.150 --> 00:45:47.070
I'm coming in!

00:45:48.160 --> 00:45:48.970
Hey, you!

00:45:50.120 --> 00:45:51.510
This is a nice apartment!

00:45:51.970 --> 00:45:53.870
And it seems to be a really quiet neighborhood.

00:45:55.620 --> 00:45:56.600
Wait, you…

00:45:57.410 --> 00:46:00.650
How can you go suddenly barging into people's homes?

00:46:00.650 --> 00:46:01.360
What do you want?

00:46:01.900 --> 00:46:03.210
Singing lessons.

00:46:03.550 --> 00:46:05.070
I was thinking of some intensive training.

00:46:07.000 --> 00:46:08.730
Now that you mention it…

00:46:08.730 --> 00:46:10.040
You're that tone-deaf boy.

00:46:10.700 --> 00:46:11.790
But I can't today.

00:46:12.180 --> 00:46:13.580
Are you going out?

00:46:14.750 --> 00:46:17.980
I've heard that on the day before an important concert or recording…

00:46:17.980 --> 00:46:20.810
You always go soak in the forest air to refresh yourself.

00:46:21.320 --> 00:46:23.000
Since you already know, why are you still here?

00:46:23.620 --> 00:46:25.860
I was thinking of going along too.

00:46:25.860 --> 00:46:26.850
Sheesh…

00:46:26.850 --> 00:46:28.140
Didn't I say so earlier?

00:46:29.040 --> 00:46:32.970
I have bad luck when I'm around you guys, so just stay away.

00:46:33.780 --> 00:46:36.090
So if you keep your distance from us…

00:46:36.090 --> 00:46:37.950
You will guarantee our safety.

00:46:39.070 --> 00:46:42.110
That's because you believe you're the one the culprit's after.

00:46:44.180 --> 00:46:46.550
When you said you wanted to go to Genta's house back then…

00:46:47.130 --> 00:46:49.530
It wasn't to complain to his parents…

00:46:49.530 --> 00:46:51.990
But to ensure Genta reached home safely, right?

00:46:53.030 --> 00:46:54.540
What kind of stupid talk is this?

00:46:55.150 --> 00:46:57.920
Oh yeah, can I have some juice before you go out?

00:46:57.920 --> 00:46:58.870
I'm thirsty.

00:47:00.490 --> 00:47:01.540
I suppose I must…

00:47:04.370 --> 00:47:06.650
It'll have to be 100% orange juice.

00:47:07.030 --> 00:47:08.340
Don't ask for the moon.

00:47:08.670 --> 00:47:10.300
Yeah, that's fine.

00:47:12.100 --> 00:47:12.970
A flute.

00:47:13.540 --> 00:47:15.050
And that man is…

00:47:16.130 --> 00:47:16.430
Hey!

00:47:18.590 --> 00:47:21.810
It's ten years too soon for you to be interested in a lady's bedroom!

00:47:22.240 --> 00:47:24.850
Say, Reiko-san, do you play the flute too?

00:47:24.850 --> 00:47:26.400
That's none of your business.

00:47:26.980 --> 00:47:28.440
Go home as soon as you're done drinking that.

00:47:29.020 --> 00:47:30.300
I'm not giving you any singing lessons…

00:47:30.920 --> 00:47:32.510
Nor am I taking you along to the forest.

00:47:35.410 --> 00:47:36.380
OK…

00:47:48.950 --> 00:47:51.180
I'm just following you on my own. Don't mind me.

00:47:52.430 --> 00:47:52.930
Whatever…

00:47:53.690 --> 00:47:55.350
It's not my fault if you get lost.

00:47:57.670 --> 00:47:58.840
No worries, no worries.

00:48:02.980 --> 00:48:03.670
Inspector Megure!

00:48:05.330 --> 00:48:07.530
We've found the connection between Akiba-san and those four.

00:48:07.750 --> 00:48:08.350
What?

00:48:09.130 --> 00:48:10.110
Three years ago, in January…

00:48:10.800 --> 00:48:14.060
At a Doumoto Academy lodging house in Izu…

00:48:14.060 --> 00:48:16.700
A flute player who was lodging with them…

00:48:17.130 --> 00:48:21.410
Got drunk, fell from a nearby cliff, and passed away.

00:48:21.660 --> 00:48:24.290
Souma Hikaru-san, age twenty-eight at the time.

00:48:24.530 --> 00:48:26.590
He was in Doumoto Academy's 6th class.

00:48:27.470 --> 00:48:28.750
Could it be that they…

00:48:29.230 --> 00:48:30.040
Yeah.

00:48:30.040 --> 00:48:33.810
They forced him to drink, even though he couldn't hold his liquor…

00:48:34.440 --> 00:48:39.470
As this had no direct relation with the fall, it was handled as an unfortunate accident.

00:48:39.930 --> 00:48:41.220
I see.

00:48:41.220 --> 00:48:43.600
Then, what's the link with Akiba-san?

00:48:44.050 --> 00:48:47.980
The thing is, this person, Souma-san, was Akiba-san's fiancé.

00:48:48.320 --> 00:48:48.910
What?

00:48:49.320 --> 00:48:49.950
Inspector…

00:48:51.200 --> 00:48:55.470
That does mean it's likely that she would have a grudge against those four.

00:48:56.600 --> 00:48:59.910
But why would she be attacked as well?

00:49:31.610 --> 00:49:32.580
Hello!

00:49:33.090 --> 00:49:33.650
Hello.

00:49:36.380 --> 00:49:36.820
Hello.

00:49:40.810 --> 00:49:42.630
Are the two of them mother and son?

00:49:42.910 --> 00:49:44.610
They don't look alike at all.

00:49:44.950 --> 00:49:47.150
Why are they walking so far apart?

00:49:47.720 --> 00:49:49.790
Maybe he made his mother angry?

00:49:52.170 --> 00:49:52.930
Jeez…

00:49:52.930 --> 00:49:53.520
Say…

00:49:54.310 --> 00:49:58.430
Do you know why I am taking a walk through the forest on the day before a concert?

00:50:00.540 --> 00:50:03.640
I want to capture the natural world inside of me.

00:50:04.240 --> 00:50:09.540
It's because European music is born out of the natural surroundings.

00:50:20.110 --> 00:50:21.120
Do you understand what I mean?

00:50:21.780 --> 00:50:22.340
Yeah.

00:50:23.180 --> 00:50:24.380
I have a hunch that I do.

00:50:36.410 --> 00:50:37.670
Are you all right, Reiko-san!?

00:50:38.260 --> 00:50:38.860
Yeah…

00:50:45.330 --> 00:50:45.860
Run!

00:50:56.030 --> 00:50:56.690
Go on ahead!

00:50:57.790 --> 00:50:59.280
The attack came, like I expected…

00:51:09.880 --> 00:51:10.620
Damn it!

00:51:15.060 --> 00:51:15.840
About to fire…

00:51:24.860 --> 00:51:26.140
Reiko-san, this way!

00:51:27.740 --> 00:51:28.560
Why?

00:51:28.780 --> 00:51:29.780
Why didn't they shoot?

00:51:31.260 --> 00:51:32.640
What are they after?

00:51:40.150 --> 00:51:43.690
Say, don't you think we should report this to the police?

00:51:43.690 --> 00:51:44.670
We can't.

00:51:44.670 --> 00:51:47.330
I already said, if we were to take this to the police…

00:51:48.060 --> 00:51:52.890
It would take up a lot of time and interfere with tomorrow's concert, right?

00:51:52.890 --> 00:51:54.170
I understand that, but…

00:51:54.780 --> 00:51:56.250
If you understand, then keep quiet.

00:51:57.190 --> 00:51:59.830
After the concert, I will tell them properly.

00:52:00.580 --> 00:52:01.010
All right?

00:52:01.590 --> 00:52:02.400
Yes…

00:52:07.210 --> 00:52:08.100
Detective Takagi?

00:52:09.030 --> 00:52:10.290
Akiba-san?

00:52:10.290 --> 00:52:11.220
And Conan-kun?

00:52:15.750 --> 00:52:18.420
Akiba-san, where did you go?

00:52:18.420 --> 00:52:19.990
Didn't you say you wouldn't be going anywhere today?

00:52:19.990 --> 00:52:21.520
I had a date with this boy.

00:52:22.150 --> 00:52:23.240
A d-date?

00:52:23.630 --> 00:52:25.950
Akiba-san, we'd like to talk with you…

00:52:25.950 --> 00:52:26.860
Some other time.

00:52:28.150 --> 00:52:30.280
And if it's about Souma Hikaru-san?

00:52:32.640 --> 00:52:35.870
Souma Hikaru-san was your fiancé, wasn't he?

00:52:37.880 --> 00:52:38.550
Inspector…

00:52:39.200 --> 00:52:41.240
I will tell you everything that I know…

00:52:42.210 --> 00:52:45.230
But, I only ask that it be after tomorrow's concert.

00:52:51.850 --> 00:52:52.920
Say, Inspector…

00:52:53.490 --> 00:52:56.440
Did Souma-san have a mole here?

00:52:57.030 --> 00:52:59.280
Yeah, that's right, but how did you know?

00:53:00.270 --> 00:53:02.950
There's a photo of him in Reiko-san's apartment.

00:53:04.190 --> 00:53:06.120
There's one in Akiba-san's apartment?

00:53:07.650 --> 00:53:09.530
I know! How about you take me home…

00:53:09.970 --> 00:53:12.450
And I'll tell you everything there?

00:53:13.520 --> 00:53:16.290
And so, we brought Conan-kun home…

00:53:16.690 --> 00:53:23.630
But in the end, all he knew was that she had a picture of Souma-san and a flute displayed in her apartment.

00:53:24.690 --> 00:53:25.480
Jeez…

00:53:26.510 --> 00:53:27.640
But, Inspector-dono…

00:53:28.180 --> 00:53:32.040
Even if she had a motive to kill those four…

00:53:32.040 --> 00:53:34.250
That alone doesn't make her the culprit, does it?

00:53:34.250 --> 00:53:36.780
She was actually attacked by that truck.

00:53:37.820 --> 00:53:38.730
Say…

00:53:38.730 --> 00:53:43.150
Does Souma-san have any relatives who would want to avenge him?

00:53:43.510 --> 00:53:45.410
No, I don't think there's anyone.

00:53:46.370 --> 00:53:47.250
Uhm…

00:53:47.250 --> 00:53:48.620
I made some tea.

00:53:48.620 --> 00:53:49.330
Oh, thank you.

00:53:50.080 --> 00:53:50.970
Sorry to trouble you, Ran-kun.

00:53:51.390 --> 00:53:51.970
Help yourself.

00:53:56.800 --> 00:53:57.730
Let's see…

00:53:57.730 --> 00:54:01.170
His mother was reportedly unmarried, 
she passed away five years ago.

00:54:01.890 --> 00:54:03.380
He had no siblings.

00:54:03.380 --> 00:54:04.250
And his father?

00:54:04.660 --> 00:54:05.840
No, we don't know.

00:54:06.370 --> 00:54:08.200
We're uncertain as to whether he's even still alive.

00:54:09.830 --> 00:54:10.590
What's that?

00:54:15.540 --> 00:54:19.610
There's one other issue with those four that died.

00:54:20.090 --> 00:54:23.800
They once performed a concert while drunk.

00:54:23.800 --> 00:54:26.570
Afterward, they were all severely scolded by Doumoto-shi.

00:54:26.570 --> 00:54:27.880
What!?

00:54:27.880 --> 00:54:29.280
When did that happen?

00:54:29.280 --> 00:54:30.450
R-Right!

00:54:30.590 --> 00:54:31.550
Let's see…

00:54:32.580 --> 00:54:33.210
Found it.

00:54:33.810 --> 00:54:35.390
It was at a concert one year ago.

00:54:35.390 --> 00:54:38.540
The performance piece was Beethoven's Piano Quartet.

00:54:41.240 --> 00:54:42.920
I understand it now, Inspector-dono.

00:54:43.720 --> 00:54:51.350
The motive and the culprit behind the deaths of those four, the grave injuries of Kabe-san and the attacks on Akiba-san…

00:54:52.600 --> 00:54:53.680
Really, Mouri-kun!?

00:54:54.340 --> 00:54:54.880
Yes.

00:54:55.270 --> 00:54:56.630
The culprit is…

00:54:58.500 --> 00:54:59.770
Doumoto Genya-san…

00:55:00.150 --> 00:55:01.060
It's you!

00:55:05.360 --> 00:55:06.580
The reason is…

00:55:06.580 --> 00:55:08.240
You're an avid Beethoven fan.

00:55:09.020 --> 00:55:09.490
And…

00:55:10.890 --> 00:55:14.410
To the point of being an extremist!

00:55:18.350 --> 00:55:19.120
Hey, hey…

00:55:19.640 --> 00:55:21.330
What are you talking about all of a sudden?

00:55:21.990 --> 00:55:28.010
You murdered the four of them because they got drunk and performed Beethoven's work so poorly.

00:55:28.290 --> 00:55:32.400
It was an insult to the great composer.

00:55:32.830 --> 00:55:41.150
You injured Kabe-san because when you last performed together, her interpretation of the piece completely opposed yours.

00:55:42.870 --> 00:55:46.450
This was also mentioned in great detail in Kabe-san's short essays collection.

00:55:47.120 --> 00:55:50.950
Finally, you attacked Akiba-san because she said, during rehearsal…

00:55:52.740 --> 00:55:54.640
I hope it isn't the 9th (daiku).

00:55:55.140 --> 00:55:56.910
I don't like that one.

00:55:57.970 --> 00:56:00.830
That was an insult to Beethoven's 9th.

00:56:02.720 --> 00:56:03.950
Hold on a minute please!

00:56:04.350 --> 00:56:05.920
Indeed, I like Beethoven…

00:56:06.180 --> 00:56:09.620
And I respect him, but I wouldn't do anything like that.

00:56:09.960 --> 00:56:11.300
No, there's no doubt about it.

00:56:12.190 --> 00:56:16.430
The fact that you have the same hairstyle as Beethoven is the proof!

00:56:19.470 --> 00:56:20.270
M-Mouri-kun?

00:56:23.800 --> 00:56:25.320
Don't joke around!

00:56:25.320 --> 00:56:26.690
This hairstyle is natural!

00:56:28.740 --> 00:56:30.290
It's just that I resemble my late mother!

00:56:30.830 --> 00:56:31.990
If you think I'm lying…

00:56:34.210 --> 00:56:34.740
Please look at this!

00:56:37.590 --> 00:56:39.120
Indeed.

00:56:39.120 --> 00:56:40.370
It's just like his.

00:56:42.040 --> 00:56:43.150
What do you think?

00:56:43.150 --> 00:56:45.030
Regarding the four victims and Akiba-san…

00:56:45.550 --> 00:56:48.990
Other than Beethoven, there is no relation whatsoever!

00:56:49.350 --> 00:56:51.720
Both Kabe-san and I are musicians.

00:56:51.910 --> 00:56:55.930
We do sometimes have vehement disputes due to differing interpretations.

00:56:56.400 --> 00:56:58.970
However, all of that is limited to the performance!

00:56:58.970 --> 00:57:01.300
We will never come to hate each other for such absurd reasons!

00:57:01.670 --> 00:57:03.640
Don't say such ridiculous things!

00:57:04.240 --> 00:57:05.460
No, I mean…

00:57:05.460 --> 00:57:06.220
Inspector!

00:57:06.820 --> 00:57:11.260
You intruded on us at this time of night just to have us listen to such a lame-brained deduction?

00:57:12.360 --> 00:57:15.450
Furthermore, there's a very important concert tomorrow.

00:57:17.000 --> 00:57:17.910
That's very true.

00:57:19.040 --> 00:57:20.950
In any case, please leave for tonight.

00:57:21.510 --> 00:57:26.190
When the concert is over, we will answer any questions to your satisfaction.

00:57:27.810 --> 00:57:31.300
Gee, I really thought I was right.

00:57:31.800 --> 00:57:34.130
Where did you get that confidence from?

00:57:35.180 --> 00:57:36.540
Say, Detective Takagi…

00:57:36.870 --> 00:57:39.500
Kabe-san still hasn't recovered her memories?

00:57:39.500 --> 00:57:41.100
Yeah, that's right.

00:57:41.100 --> 00:57:44.020
She's starting to be able to chat about things, but…

00:57:44.380 --> 00:57:48.790
She's saying stuff like how she notices the pitch of the sound the air conditioner makes and can't sleep.

00:57:48.790 --> 00:57:51.480
She's sure saying some incomprehensible things, huh?

00:57:52.510 --> 00:57:54.540
The pitch in the sound of the air-conditioner?

00:57:55.310 --> 00:57:56.170
Could it be…

00:58:00.080 --> 00:58:02.450
You don't have to take it out now.

00:58:02.590 --> 00:58:03.950
Oh, sorry.

00:58:03.950 --> 00:58:04.770
Please, use this.

00:58:05.110 --> 00:58:05.410
Yes.

00:58:07.070 --> 00:58:09.990
It will be exactly the same as the public performance.

00:58:09.990 --> 00:58:15.830
To be able to choose your seat in an empty concert hall and listen to them play makes dress rehearsals worthwhile.

00:58:24.700 --> 00:58:26.810
Our seats for the public performance are upstairs.

00:58:27.410 --> 00:58:28.940
I asked Papa to get them.

00:58:30.780 --> 00:58:32.180
You mean balcony seats?

00:58:32.580 --> 00:58:36.070
There are a total of ten seats, all reserved for us.

00:58:36.930 --> 00:58:38.010
Ten of us?

00:58:38.250 --> 00:58:40.660
I invited Professor Agasa and the kids as well.

00:58:41.200 --> 00:58:42.880
And one more for Shinichi-kun…

00:58:44.840 --> 00:58:45.900
Let him know about it.

00:58:46.410 --> 00:58:48.650
The ticket will be left at the reception desk.

00:58:49.150 --> 00:58:50.440
There's no need to worry about him.

00:58:50.800 --> 00:58:53.880
It's all right. Hurry, or the seat will be wasted!

00:58:54.080 --> 00:58:55.460
I guess I have no choice.

00:58:55.980 --> 00:58:57.380
But I don't think he'll come.

00:58:59.590 --> 00:59:00.740
I'm sorry, Ran.

00:59:07.500 --> 00:59:10.690
About yesterday, it seems you kept it from the police.

00:59:11.380 --> 00:59:13.060
You have my gratitude for that.

00:59:13.510 --> 00:59:15.120
Don't worry about that…

00:59:15.120 --> 00:59:16.560
How's the wound on your leg?

00:59:17.710 --> 00:59:19.170
It won't affect my singing.

00:59:20.360 --> 00:59:21.220
Say…

00:59:21.220 --> 00:59:24.330
Kabe Souko-san has perfect pitch as well, doesn't she?

00:59:24.900 --> 00:59:28.320
Yeah, I figured that out when we met face to face.

00:59:28.320 --> 00:59:29.790
We got along pretty well.

00:59:30.560 --> 00:59:31.380
Does that mean anything?

00:59:32.700 --> 00:59:33.750
It's nothing.

00:59:34.960 --> 00:59:35.420
Oh?

00:59:37.160 --> 00:59:38.050
Well, I have to go.

00:59:39.380 --> 00:59:40.770
Good luck with the concert.

00:59:44.950 --> 00:59:47.790
Both Reiko-san and Kabe-san have perfect pitch.

00:59:48.660 --> 00:59:49.350
That means…

00:59:50.320 --> 00:59:53.330
I'll get upset if we talk over the phone, so I just sent an e-mail.

00:59:53.680 --> 00:59:54.560
Oh?

00:59:54.560 --> 00:59:56.190
It'll be good if Shinichi-kun can come.

00:59:57.160 --> 00:59:59.400
I'm fine with it either way.

00:59:59.840 --> 01:00:01.410
It's just that the seat will be wasted…

01:00:01.930 --> 01:00:03.910
That's what I said before.

01:00:03.910 --> 01:00:04.810
Oh, really?

01:00:05.540 --> 01:00:08.190
It can't be helped, let's start without him.

01:00:10.780 --> 01:00:11.830
Is something wrong?

01:00:12.570 --> 01:00:13.560
Oh, Mouri-san.

01:00:14.160 --> 01:00:15.920
Müller-san hasn't come.

01:00:16.700 --> 01:00:17.970
You mean the organ tuner?

01:00:18.650 --> 01:00:22.300
We agreed that he would be present at the dress rehearsal to do any fine tuning.

01:00:22.780 --> 01:00:24.320
Jeez, this is really troublesome!

01:00:25.470 --> 01:00:30.180
He didn't take any of my calls, and the hotel staff said he hasn't returned since last night.

01:00:31.370 --> 01:00:32.140
Since last night?

01:00:33.030 --> 01:00:38.460
Well, it's only the fine tuning that's left, so it won't be a problem even if he doesn't come.

01:00:38.800 --> 01:00:41.100
But doesn't that mean he's gone missing?

01:00:41.490 --> 01:00:43.110
Have you reported this to the police?

01:00:43.670 --> 01:00:44.100
No.

01:00:44.660 --> 01:00:48.100
It'll be troublesome, since the questioning will take quite a bit of time.

01:00:48.860 --> 01:00:51.970
For now, we want to concentrate on the concert.

01:01:04.880 --> 01:01:06.800
Shion-san seems like a completely different person.

01:01:18.730 --> 01:01:27.730
♪ Ave Maria
Charles-Francois Gounod

01:02:28.820 --> 01:02:30.020
Her voice…

01:02:52.210 --> 01:02:54.660
Shion-san's violin playing was fantastic!

01:02:54.660 --> 01:02:57.760
Really! It was completely different from the last rehearsal!

01:02:58.500 --> 01:03:02.270
She really made that Stradivarius her own!

01:03:02.460 --> 01:03:03.550
What would you know about it?

01:03:04.330 --> 01:03:06.830
Not to mention, Reiko-san's singing was wonderful!

01:03:11.870 --> 01:03:13.020
Conan-kun!

01:03:16.650 --> 01:03:18.120
You guys are way too early.

01:03:18.550 --> 01:03:21.140
That's because you aren't allowed in even if you're only a minute late.

01:03:21.800 --> 01:03:23.820
We asked the professor to bring us here early.

01:03:24.280 --> 01:03:26.150
Hey, what's that you're holding?

01:03:27.660 --> 01:03:28.860
Isn't that a recorder?

01:03:29.400 --> 01:03:31.150
Are you an idiot?

01:03:31.150 --> 01:03:34.490
Who would bring something like that to a classical concert?

01:03:34.490 --> 01:03:35.910
Don't scold him.

01:03:35.910 --> 01:03:39.960
Genta-kun can't talk, so he wanted to at least make some sounds.

01:03:39.960 --> 01:03:41.170
Even so…

01:03:41.730 --> 01:03:44.480
Of course, he won't play it during the performance.

01:03:45.020 --> 01:03:46.030
Isn't that right, Genta?

01:03:48.340 --> 01:03:50.250
That means “yes”.

01:03:51.870 --> 01:03:53.530
Keep it hidden when you're in the hall!

01:03:54.710 --> 01:03:56.810
Cellphones are forbidden too.

01:03:57.170 --> 01:03:58.510
They know.

01:03:58.510 --> 01:04:00.850
They even left their detective badges behind.

01:04:01.110 --> 01:04:02.730
Hey, I'm hungry.

01:04:05.370 --> 01:04:07.200
Well, if we're hungry, let's get something to eat.

01:04:07.720 --> 01:04:08.680
Sounds good.

01:04:08.680 --> 01:04:12.110
The performance is at 5:00, and it wouldn't do if our stomachs were growling then.

01:04:16.080 --> 01:04:17.740
He's saying “eel rice”, “eel rice”!

01:04:18.600 --> 01:04:21.580
If only you could hold a conversation with a recorder, huh?

01:04:21.590 --> 01:04:24.000
Well, it's not like you couldn't do it.

01:04:24.820 --> 01:04:26.800
All you have to do is to change the notes into letters.

01:04:27.170 --> 01:04:28.080
Change the notes…

01:04:28.380 --> 01:04:29.970
Into letters?

01:04:31.420 --> 01:04:35.010
However, I mean using the alphabet, so Kojima-kun wouldn't be able to do that yet.

01:04:35.430 --> 01:04:37.270
That sound is bothering me…

01:04:37.660 --> 01:04:40.770
Ran-neechan, I just remembered that there's something I have to do.

01:04:41.240 --> 01:04:43.410
I promise I'll be in my seat before the curtain rises.

01:04:45.010 --> 01:04:46.320
Wait, Conan-kun!

01:04:46.840 --> 01:04:48.860
What a selfish brat…

01:05:10.250 --> 01:05:11.570
That note!

01:05:11.570 --> 01:05:12.880
Isn't that note a little flat?

01:05:13.140 --> 01:05:13.880
Yeah.

01:05:13.880 --> 01:05:14.850
I have the same feeling.

01:05:15.550 --> 01:05:17.350
I noticed it while singing.

01:05:17.920 --> 01:05:20.120
But, even though I know which key it is…

01:05:20.740 --> 01:05:23.020
I don't know which stop and timbre it was.

01:05:23.830 --> 01:05:25.650
That's because there were several pipes sounding at the same time.

01:05:31.650 --> 01:05:33.580
It does sound slightly flat.

01:05:33.580 --> 01:05:34.650
There's no doubt about it.

01:05:34.980 --> 01:05:36.760
It's coming from somewhere in that area.

01:05:37.260 --> 01:05:40.120
I think it's probably one of the short, inner pipes.

01:05:40.820 --> 01:05:43.250
One of them must have gone out of tune.

01:05:43.910 --> 01:05:46.080
It will need tuning prior to the performance.

01:05:46.650 --> 01:05:50.090
But aren't Müller-san's whereabouts unknown?

01:05:50.090 --> 01:05:50.830
That's true.

01:05:51.090 --> 01:05:52.300
At any rate, we have to inform Doumoto-san…

01:06:00.860 --> 01:06:02.180
He doesn't seem to be in.

01:06:02.760 --> 01:06:03.430
Guess not.

01:06:03.950 --> 01:06:05.920
Perhaps he went out for tea or something?

01:06:06.800 --> 01:06:08.400
Or maybe he's there…

01:06:08.960 --> 01:06:11.930
But, you know, I'm surprised you noticed the note.

01:06:13.690 --> 01:06:15.430
My ears are sharp.

01:06:16.010 --> 01:06:17.440
They're more than good.

01:06:17.870 --> 01:06:20.690
Maybe you have perfect pitch too.

01:06:20.920 --> 01:06:22.040
If only that were so.

01:06:28.710 --> 01:06:30.790
Doumoto-san doesn't seem to be here…

01:06:32.530 --> 01:06:34.840
Do you know of any other places where he might be?

01:06:37.090 --> 01:06:38.270
Not really…

01:06:38.270 --> 01:06:40.390
Maybe he did go out for tea, just like you said.

01:07:03.520 --> 01:07:06.120
Ladies and gentlemen, your attention please.

01:07:06.880 --> 01:07:10.850
Please bear in mind that smoking is permitted only in the designated areas.

01:07:08.390 --> 01:07:10.040
Akiba-san's still not here?

01:07:10.370 --> 01:07:10.900
No.

01:07:11.480 --> 01:07:13.300
I called her cellphone but no one picked up.

01:07:13.990 --> 01:07:16.410
I have the staff searching the area for her as well, but…

01:07:16.410 --> 01:07:17.880
Could she have gone missing?

01:07:18.390 --> 01:07:19.200
I don't know.

01:07:19.780 --> 01:07:21.830
Müller-san, and now even her…

01:07:22.680 --> 01:07:24.180
Why the heck is this happening?

01:07:24.570 --> 01:07:26.390
There are only fifteen minutes until the performance.

01:07:27.120 --> 01:07:29.440
If she doesn't turn up by then…

01:07:29.440 --> 01:07:30.980
Please allow me to take her place.

01:07:33.040 --> 01:07:34.740
Because of what happened to Kabe-san…

01:07:35.320 --> 01:07:38.530
I thought that something like this might happen too…

01:07:39.210 --> 01:07:41.380
And I've been practicing very hard.

01:07:42.850 --> 01:07:43.660
But…

01:07:45.450 --> 01:07:46.920
I beg you, Sensei!

01:07:47.230 --> 01:07:49.870
I promise I'll sing better than Akiba-san!

01:07:49.870 --> 01:07:52.540
There's no need for you to sing better than her.

01:07:54.160 --> 01:07:57.140
Music is the connection between us humans and God.

01:07:58.450 --> 01:07:59.920
You must sing as though in prayer.

01:08:08.650 --> 01:08:10.930
Shinichi-kun didn't turn up after all…

01:08:12.090 --> 01:08:14.370
Even so, what's happened to Conan-kun?

01:08:14.560 --> 01:08:15.980
It's going to start soon…

01:08:16.640 --> 01:08:19.430
Really, where could Conan-kun have gone?

01:08:21.010 --> 01:08:22.950
Still, since it's Conan-kun, I'm sure he'll be all right.

01:08:23.320 --> 01:08:24.990
I believe in him.

01:08:25.500 --> 01:08:26.310
That's right.

01:08:26.800 --> 01:08:29.350
Just like Conan-kun believed in us…

01:08:30.080 --> 01:08:30.830
We have to too!

01:08:32.870 --> 01:08:35.680
Conan-kun will definitely be all right.

01:08:39.650 --> 01:08:41.930
Ladies and gentlemen, your attention please.

01:08:42.470 --> 01:08:46.220
Due to unforseen circumstances, Akiba Reiko…

01:08:46.220 --> 01:08:48.140
Will not be performing today.

01:08:50.850 --> 01:08:55.650
She is being replaced by Chigusa Rara, of Doumoto Music Academy's 9th class.

01:08:56.500 --> 01:09:00.400
We seek your understanding on this matter.

01:09:01.180 --> 01:09:02.180
Why?

01:09:02.470 --> 01:09:05.200
But she sang so well during the dress rehearsal!

01:09:06.630 --> 01:09:09.180
Could it be that she and Shinichi are in trouble?

01:09:18.760 --> 01:09:19.760
A vinyl sheet?

01:09:20.120 --> 01:09:20.710
What?

01:09:31.950 --> 01:09:32.560
Reiko-san!

01:09:32.740 --> 01:09:33.310
Reiko-san!

01:09:40.160 --> 01:09:40.610
What!?

01:09:42.010 --> 01:09:43.710
Where are we?

01:09:44.130 --> 01:09:45.570
This is probably downstream on the canal.

01:09:46.780 --> 01:09:48.710
The culprit who attacked us…

01:09:48.710 --> 01:09:51.840
Set us adrift from the lake behind Doumoto Hall and let the canal carry us here.

01:09:52.460 --> 01:09:53.970
But, who would…

01:09:54.590 --> 01:09:55.330
I don't know.

01:09:56.720 --> 01:10:00.550
Moreover, why did he bother to put us in a boat after knocking us out?

01:10:00.970 --> 01:10:03.130
Anyway, if we don't return soon…

01:10:03.130 --> 01:10:03.830
The concert will be…

01:10:04.290 --> 01:10:06.750
But, even if we were to swim across…

01:10:06.750 --> 01:10:08.760
That wall is too high for us to climb.

01:10:24.040 --> 01:10:25.470
There doesn't seem to be anyone around.

01:10:27.860 --> 01:10:28.830
But, look!

01:10:28.830 --> 01:10:30.700
There's a telephone on that wall over there!

01:10:32.720 --> 01:10:35.200
If we can reach it, we can call for help…

01:10:36.480 --> 01:10:37.290
Hold on a second.

01:10:38.010 --> 01:10:39.820
Even if we can't reach the phone…

01:10:39.820 --> 01:10:41.920
If we can remove the receiver, we may be able to call for help.

01:10:42.490 --> 01:10:44.130
How are we going to do that?

01:10:44.930 --> 01:10:47.150
When you dial the numbers to make a call…

01:10:47.150 --> 01:10:48.830
It makes those ''pi, po, pa'' sounds, right?

01:10:49.260 --> 01:10:52.130
That's known as the DTMF signal.

01:10:52.630 --> 01:10:55.450
It uses a combination of both a high and a low signal…

01:10:55.450 --> 01:10:57.380
To transmit the telephone number.

01:10:58.610 --> 01:11:01.230
So, if we can successfully produce those sounds…

01:11:01.230 --> 01:11:02.940
We can make a call, right?

01:11:04.290 --> 01:11:09.320
The ''1'' in the emergency number ''110'' is 697 Hertz and 1209 Hertz.

01:11:09.860 --> 01:11:15.660
''0'' should be a combination of 941 Hertz and 1336 Hertz.

01:11:16.080 --> 01:11:16.760
All right.

01:11:17.130 --> 01:11:19.660
I can remember the dial sounds.

01:11:20.390 --> 01:11:22.630
But first, we have to get the receiver off…

01:11:23.140 --> 01:11:24.180
Leave that to me.

01:11:25.150 --> 01:11:28.730
However, the problem is that after the receiver is off for a while…

01:11:29.050 --> 01:11:31.090
You can no longer make a call.

01:11:31.920 --> 01:11:34.050
That means we can only challenge this once.

01:11:34.620 --> 01:11:38.600
If we fail, we'll have to wait until someone finds us.

01:11:39.280 --> 01:11:40.790
We don't have any time to waste.

01:11:41.250 --> 01:11:42.340
Let's do it!

01:11:44.390 --> 01:11:45.530
Since we've decided…

01:11:45.530 --> 01:11:47.190
Let's have a quick rehearsal!

01:11:50.060 --> 01:11:51.070
What was that just now?

01:11:51.490 --> 01:11:52.090
An explosion…

01:11:52.780 --> 01:11:53.700
Something exploded!

01:11:56.390 --> 01:11:57.750
It was in the direction of Doumoto Hall!

01:11:58.970 --> 01:11:59.520
Could it be…

01:12:09.730 --> 01:12:11.890
We are on-scene at Nishitama City's Music Woods.

01:12:12.470 --> 01:12:16.590
Just moments ago, two explosions occurred here at the Doumoto Hall.

01:12:17.550 --> 01:12:19.530
The explosions were at the innermost section on the left and…

01:12:19.530 --> 01:12:21.810
At the stage door, center section on the right.

01:12:22.020 --> 01:12:23.970
The concert began five minutes ago.

01:12:23.970 --> 01:12:24.690
The situation inside is currently…

01:12:30.780 --> 01:12:31.460
Another one…

01:12:31.780 --> 01:12:33.290
Hurry! Next is the sound for ''0''!

01:12:40.960 --> 01:12:41.540
That should do it.

01:12:42.270 --> 01:12:43.040
Let's row the boat over.

01:12:52.710 --> 01:12:53.610
This will do.

01:12:53.610 --> 01:12:54.260
Stop the boat.

01:12:57.360 --> 01:12:59.680
So, how do you intend to remove the receiver?

01:13:00.060 --> 01:13:00.980
Just wait and see.

01:13:15.260 --> 01:13:15.910
Amazing!

01:13:16.480 --> 01:13:17.080
Let's do it!

01:13:25.990 --> 01:13:28.670
Hello, this is the 110 communication headquarters.

01:13:33.490 --> 01:13:34.960
Akiba-san and Conan-kun are?

01:13:35.490 --> 01:13:35.720
Yeah.

01:13:36.570 --> 01:13:40.930
It seems they were knocked out by someone, placed in a boat, and washed downstream on the canal.

01:13:41.530 --> 01:13:45.020
The location is in Nishitama City, at the Nishitama Reservoir Sluice Gate Operations Center.

01:13:50.380 --> 01:13:51.070
They're here!

01:13:54.260 --> 01:13:55.350
I see them!

01:13:55.350 --> 01:13:56.030
Over there!

01:14:05.050 --> 01:14:06.420
It really was Doumoto Hall?

01:14:07.600 --> 01:14:09.900
There have been over ten explosions so far…

01:14:09.900 --> 01:14:12.210
All of which were on the external pillars of the building.

01:14:12.210 --> 01:14:13.370
The cause is still…

01:14:13.800 --> 01:14:15.770
Someone planted bombs there.

01:14:16.460 --> 01:14:18.900
Even though we don't know whether they're on a timer or remote-controlled…

01:14:19.630 --> 01:14:23.350
Most likely, we're dealing with the same person responsible for killing the four musicians.

01:14:23.820 --> 01:14:24.810
Exactly.

01:14:24.810 --> 01:14:27.110
The first incident was also an explosion.

01:14:28.190 --> 01:14:28.870
But…

01:14:29.520 --> 01:14:32.870
Why didn't he just kill us instead of sending us away from the concert hall?

01:14:35.900 --> 01:14:36.860
Could it be that she…

01:14:42.850 --> 01:14:43.590
Another one.

01:14:44.130 --> 01:14:44.690
Say…

01:14:45.480 --> 01:14:46.870
Can't you contact anyone inside?

01:14:47.450 --> 01:14:49.050
Ran-neechan, Uncle and the others are all in there.

01:14:49.290 --> 01:14:51.380
Yes, but we can't get through…

01:14:51.920 --> 01:14:53.590
The culprit may have cut the lines.

01:14:54.010 --> 01:14:55.310
But what about cellphones?

01:14:55.310 --> 01:14:55.930
That won't work.

01:14:57.250 --> 01:14:59.800
It's courteous to switch off cellphones during the performance.

01:15:00.220 --> 01:15:02.560
The interior of the hall is out of range aside from one area.

01:15:03.160 --> 01:15:06.350
Besides, I think it should be all right inside.

01:15:08.070 --> 01:15:11.540
The interior of the concert hall is entirely soundproof and fireproof.

01:15:12.470 --> 01:15:15.290
It's possible that they haven't even noticed the explosions.

01:15:16.920 --> 01:15:19.100
In that case, the possibility that the concert is still in progress is…

01:15:19.510 --> 01:15:20.170
Yeah.

01:15:20.170 --> 01:15:21.240
It's possible, I'd imagine.

01:15:21.680 --> 01:15:24.700
But, the explosions will not be limited to the exterior forever…

01:15:25.820 --> 01:15:26.750
They'll eventually occur inside too…

01:15:27.580 --> 01:15:28.080
No…

01:15:28.880 --> 01:15:30.300
It may have already happened!

01:15:32.550 --> 01:15:33.050
Ran…

01:15:36.170 --> 01:15:44.170
♪ Jesu, Joy of Man's Desiring
Johann Sebastian Bach
Cantata, BWV 147, Chorale No.6

01:17:01.580 --> 01:17:02.970
Ladies and gentlemen, good evening.

01:17:03.470 --> 01:17:05.520
A warm welcome to all of you here tonight.

01:17:06.260 --> 01:17:07.840
I am Doumoto Kazuki.

01:17:10.780 --> 01:17:14.770
As you are all aware, in this very hall on this very night, this pipe organ…

01:17:16.300 --> 01:17:17.220
Hurry!

01:17:17.220 --> 01:17:18.070
Quickly, over here!

01:17:18.580 --> 01:17:19.430
What are you doing?

01:17:19.740 --> 01:17:21.150
Hurry and get that hose over here!

01:17:31.880 --> 01:17:32.580
This is bad…

01:17:32.990 --> 01:17:35.710
But the center section seems to be unharmed.

01:17:36.280 --> 01:17:38.170
The people inside should be all right.

01:17:38.600 --> 01:17:40.030
It's still too early to rejoice.

01:17:41.220 --> 01:17:43.970
All of the access points to the outside have been sealed!

01:17:44.440 --> 01:17:45.720
A rescue operation is impossible!

01:17:46.000 --> 01:17:46.700
No way!

01:17:47.120 --> 01:17:50.370
Moreover, we don't even know which pillar will explode next.

01:17:50.990 --> 01:17:53.540
There are a total of 23 pillars on the exterior.

01:17:54.040 --> 01:17:56.150
Perhaps they're planning on blowing them all up.

01:17:56.630 --> 01:17:58.370
Damn it, what should we do?

01:17:59.340 --> 01:18:01.080
We can only get in from the rooftop…

01:18:02.260 --> 01:18:02.960
Is that possible?

01:18:03.310 --> 01:18:04.650
It should be possible, for now.

01:18:05.440 --> 01:18:08.170
However, there isn't a proper heliport.

01:18:08.560 --> 01:18:11.080
We don't know if the roof will be able to withstand the weight of the helicopter or not…

01:18:11.540 --> 01:18:12.240
Very well.

01:18:12.890 --> 01:18:14.940
Please descend to the lowest possible height.

01:18:15.480 --> 01:18:16.560
We'll jump from there.

01:18:17.920 --> 01:18:19.230
I'll show you the way.

01:18:20.360 --> 01:18:23.510
The passageway from the roof to the fourth level is complicated.

01:18:23.720 --> 01:18:24.410
Therefore…

01:18:25.070 --> 01:18:26.160
But, that's…

01:18:26.160 --> 01:18:27.740
There's no time for arguments, right?

01:18:28.200 --> 01:18:30.670
We have to hurry while the explosions have stopped!

01:18:36.670 --> 01:18:37.600
Go lower!

01:18:39.220 --> 01:18:39.900
More!

01:18:40.900 --> 01:18:41.770
Just a little more!

01:18:44.230 --> 01:18:45.120
A little more!

01:18:46.590 --> 01:18:47.790
I can't go any farther!

01:18:48.140 --> 01:18:50.070
The turbulence is worse than I expected!

01:18:50.070 --> 01:18:51.110
I can't keep it steady!

01:18:52.660 --> 01:18:54.200
If you want to go, go now!

01:18:58.070 --> 01:18:59.290
Come on, Akiba-san!

01:19:06.150 --> 01:19:08.850
Now, Conan-kun, stay in the helicopter and…

01:19:09.870 --> 01:19:10.720
Conan-kun!

01:19:11.410 --> 01:19:12.670
I'm staying here!

01:19:12.980 --> 01:19:15.530
Until Ran-neechan and everyone else have been rescued!

01:19:15.960 --> 01:19:16.680
Conan-kun!

01:19:17.250 --> 01:19:19.150
And, I saw the culprit's face!

01:19:20.850 --> 01:19:22.550
Even though we don't know the culprit behind the explosions…

01:19:23.090 --> 01:19:24.730
I saw the one who attacked us!

01:19:25.490 --> 01:19:27.570
Isn't it possible that he's inside the concert hall?

01:19:27.570 --> 01:19:27.900
So…

01:19:31.460 --> 01:19:33.080
Hurry! I can't hold it much longer!

01:19:33.610 --> 01:19:35.760
It can't be helped; we'll have to bring him along.

01:19:36.340 --> 01:19:37.640
Takagi-kun, hurry!

01:19:37.900 --> 01:19:38.290
Right!

01:19:57.060 --> 01:19:58.650
This is an internal corridor on the fourth floor.

01:19:59.380 --> 01:20:02.400
Didn't we simply descend directly from the top?

01:20:03.030 --> 01:20:05.270
If I didn't say that, you wouldn't have allowed me to come along, would you?

01:20:05.740 --> 01:20:06.780
It's the same with this boy.

01:20:08.420 --> 01:20:10.990
Did you really see the culprit's face?

01:20:21.920 --> 01:20:29.920
♪ He Shall Feed His Flock
George Frideric Handel
Messiah, HWV 56

01:20:30.060 --> 01:20:31.140
This is surprising.

01:20:31.720 --> 01:20:35.390
It was a possibility, but to think that they really haven't noticed the explosions…

01:20:35.970 --> 01:20:36.510
Yeah.

01:20:37.210 --> 01:20:39.140
Anyway, let's search for the bombs.

01:20:39.720 --> 01:20:42.690
It won't be possible to evacuate so many people.

01:20:43.320 --> 01:20:46.140
Above all, if the objective was to destroy this concert hall…

01:20:46.670 --> 01:20:49.490
There should be bombs installed in here as well.

01:20:50.060 --> 01:20:50.800
Got it.

01:20:51.410 --> 01:20:54.810
Conan-kun, wait here with Akiba-san.

01:20:55.020 --> 01:20:55.720
All right.

01:20:56.130 --> 01:20:56.830
Let's go.

01:20:56.830 --> 01:20:57.350
Yes.

01:21:06.780 --> 01:21:07.500
Ran…

01:21:09.840 --> 01:21:10.820
Wait for me.

01:21:20.390 --> 01:21:21.190
How is it?

01:21:21.620 --> 01:21:23.100
What's the situation inside?

01:22:01.960 --> 01:22:05.090
The culprit, knowing the structure of the hall very well…

01:22:05.440 --> 01:22:07.340
Placed the bombs accordingly.

01:22:09.460 --> 01:22:11.900
It is probably one of the staff.

01:22:15.370 --> 01:22:17.250
That note really does sound strange.

01:22:18.420 --> 01:22:19.740
Even Doumoto-san didn't notice it…

01:22:20.230 --> 01:22:22.040
He'd probably notice if it was piano, but…

01:22:22.580 --> 01:22:26.210
He's only been playing the organ for the last two years, so he probably can't tell the difference…

01:22:27.930 --> 01:22:28.970
The difference in sound…

01:22:29.590 --> 01:22:32.630
''A bunch of amateurs who can't differentiate between sounds.''

01:22:33.420 --> 01:22:34.690
So that's what it was about…

01:22:35.350 --> 01:22:37.070
Kabe-san noticed the difference…

01:22:37.490 --> 01:22:39.040
Because she has perfect pitch.

01:22:39.660 --> 01:22:40.420
Wait!

01:22:40.870 --> 01:22:42.130
Then why did that person…

01:22:43.150 --> 01:22:44.930
Could it be, that person…

01:22:46.320 --> 01:22:47.240
If that's the case…

01:22:48.520 --> 01:22:49.370
Why was she…

01:22:54.500 --> 01:22:57.570
His mother was reportedly unmarried…

01:22:58.530 --> 01:23:01.000
I see. So that's how it is.

01:23:01.500 --> 01:23:04.980
But, what does the difference in sound have to do with the explosions?

01:23:08.270 --> 01:23:10.330
Hey, it just occurred to me, but…

01:23:10.980 --> 01:23:12.870
When the explosions stopped earlier…

01:23:13.510 --> 01:23:16.300
It was during Doumoto-san's speech, wasn't it?

01:23:17.370 --> 01:23:20.320
Perhaps it was really because they didn't want people to notice the explosions?

01:23:21.200 --> 01:23:22.630
No, that's not it!

01:23:23.360 --> 01:23:25.410
The explosions will not occur unless the performance is underway!

01:23:26.500 --> 01:23:28.930
I got it! So that's why the note sounded strange!

01:23:30.750 --> 01:23:31.600
It's that note again…

01:23:33.050 --> 01:23:34.530
Say, how many times has it sounded?

01:23:35.540 --> 01:23:37.160
From the start of the concert up to now…

01:23:37.620 --> 01:23:39.490
Do you know how many times that off-key note has sounded?

01:23:39.870 --> 01:23:41.220
Let's see, I think it was…

01:23:41.680 --> 01:23:43.450
Twice during the first Ave Maria…

01:23:48.180 --> 01:23:49.720
And during the Cantata after that…

01:23:51.050 --> 01:23:52.080
Ten times.

01:24:04.240 --> 01:24:07.010
And, eight times for the current piece…

01:24:07.540 --> 01:24:08.850
That's twenty in total.

01:24:09.300 --> 01:24:11.350
Then, there are probably four more.

01:24:13.270 --> 01:24:15.550
That note is linked to the explosions.

01:24:16.050 --> 01:24:19.950
That's why no explosions occurred during Doumoto-san's speech.

01:24:31.410 --> 01:24:33.870
There are 23 pillars on the exterior of the concert hall.

01:24:34.360 --> 01:24:34.880
In other words…

01:24:35.380 --> 01:24:37.370
To destroy all the pillars…

01:24:37.370 --> 01:24:38.710
And the interior of the concert hall…

01:24:39.140 --> 01:24:41.330
24 explosions are required.

01:24:44.930 --> 01:24:45.780
That means…

01:24:47.890 --> 01:24:48.550
Exactly.

01:24:51.280 --> 01:24:54.560
If we don't stop the performance before that note sounds for the fourth time…

01:24:55.170 --> 01:24:57.660
The bomb inside the concert hall will explode.

01:25:07.050 --> 01:25:07.860
It's that note again.

01:25:08.210 --> 01:25:09.240
Damn.

01:25:09.240 --> 01:25:11.250
It really is linked to that note.

01:25:12.330 --> 01:25:14.530
The culprit should be observing from somewhere.

01:25:24.040 --> 01:25:24.800
Again!

01:25:25.400 --> 01:25:26.430
Found them…

01:25:27.430 --> 01:25:28.890
So it was that person after all.

01:25:31.960 --> 01:25:34.500
All right, I'll get on stage and stop the performance.

01:25:34.500 --> 01:25:34.850
Wait!

01:25:35.870 --> 01:25:36.790
If you don't handle it well…

01:25:37.220 --> 01:25:38.650
They'll set the explosions off via remote control.

01:25:39.220 --> 01:25:41.820
I've found him, the culprit with the remote control.

01:25:42.540 --> 01:25:43.150
But…

01:25:43.790 --> 01:25:45.170
Damn it, what should I do?

01:25:45.670 --> 01:25:48.490
Isn't there some way to stop the performance…

01:25:49.420 --> 01:25:51.860
Is there no way to stop the explosions!?

01:25:53.490 --> 01:25:54.140
Three minutes.

01:25:56.070 --> 01:25:57.330
Will three minutes be enough?

01:25:59.120 --> 01:25:59.740
But…

01:26:04.870 --> 01:26:07.260
Well, I'll leave it to you, little detective.

01:26:55.770 --> 01:26:57.100
It's Reiko-sensei!

01:26:57.470 --> 01:26:58.410
This song…

01:26:58.880 --> 01:27:00.480
It's ''Amazing Grace'', right?

01:27:24.410 --> 01:27:25.650
What's she up to now?

01:28:31.450 --> 01:28:39.450
♪ Amazing Grace
John Newton

01:29:46.120 --> 01:29:47.410
The person from that time…

01:29:47.900 --> 01:29:49.890
It really was Reiko-san.

01:29:59.890 --> 01:30:02.290
I knew I should have eliminated her back then.

01:30:02.680 --> 01:30:03.600
I won't let you erase it.

01:30:05.640 --> 01:30:08.500
Not this voice raised in song that warms people's hearts.

01:30:10.040 --> 01:30:12.050
That's why you were hesitant, right?

01:30:13.610 --> 01:30:14.870
Moreover, this song was…

01:30:15.410 --> 01:30:19.630
Your son's, Souma Hikaru-san's, most beloved song.

01:30:20.590 --> 01:30:24.960
And the person singing was the person he loved.

01:30:26.850 --> 01:30:28.420
The crux of my deduction…

01:30:28.420 --> 01:30:29.820
Lies in the irregular note.

01:30:30.440 --> 01:30:34.170
At first, we believed the irregularity was because it was out of tune.

01:30:34.710 --> 01:30:36.260
But, that wasn't so.

01:30:37.770 --> 01:30:39.580
Inside one of the organ pipes…

01:30:40.130 --> 01:30:43.840
There is a small sensor which is set to detect minute changes in air flow.

01:30:44.420 --> 01:30:48.130
Due to that, the sound generated from the pipe is slightly off.

01:30:49.110 --> 01:30:52.690
When the sensor in the pipe detects a change in air flow…

01:30:54.600 --> 01:30:59.050
It sends signals in a sequential order to the bombs you had set up earlier, which subsequently detonate.

01:31:03.760 --> 01:31:06.580
And then, when the one final bomb explodes…

01:31:07.160 --> 01:31:09.290
That will achieve your long-cherished desire to destroy this hall.

01:31:10.520 --> 01:31:12.690
There were no explosions during the dress rehearsal…

01:31:13.230 --> 01:31:15.780
Because the detonators had not yet been activated.

01:31:16.440 --> 01:31:17.530
Isn't that so?

01:31:18.560 --> 01:31:22.250
Director of Doumoto Hall and former piano tuner…

01:31:22.650 --> 01:31:24.120
Fuwa Takumi-san?

01:31:30.790 --> 01:31:31.800
There's nothing here either.

01:31:32.270 --> 01:31:33.570
This isn't good.

01:31:33.950 --> 01:31:36.940
If this continues, the bomb will explode before we locate it!

01:31:37.590 --> 01:31:38.290
Be quiet.

01:31:41.720 --> 01:31:43.110
What's that sound?

01:32:06.860 --> 01:32:07.590
Don't move!

01:32:07.940 --> 01:32:08.680
This is the police!

01:32:10.960 --> 01:32:11.950
Müller-san!

01:32:20.880 --> 01:32:23.970
How did you know it was me?

01:32:24.530 --> 01:32:25.730
Perfect pitch.

01:32:26.720 --> 01:32:29.190
Fuwa-san, even though you have perfect pitch…

01:32:29.800 --> 01:32:32.690
You didn't point out the irregular note during the dress rehearsal, did you?

01:32:34.030 --> 01:32:36.400
That made me suspicious.

01:32:39.690 --> 01:32:40.780
I see.

01:32:41.860 --> 01:32:44.570
Then, what you said about me being Hikaru's father…

01:32:45.150 --> 01:32:48.570
Your car's license plate number is 52-83.

01:32:49.170 --> 01:32:51.830
You took that from your son's birth date, didn't you?

01:32:53.600 --> 01:32:56.860
You used it as a testimony of your connection to your beloved son…

01:32:57.470 --> 01:32:59.510
Even though you could not proclaim it to the world.

01:33:00.360 --> 01:33:04.680
Moreover, that photo in Doumoto-san's house from when you were younger…

01:33:05.320 --> 01:33:06.770
Your son looked just like you.

01:33:11.640 --> 01:33:14.080
You killed those four musicians…

01:33:14.540 --> 01:33:16.940
To avenge your late son who died in the accident.

01:33:17.940 --> 01:33:19.920
You left the flute parts at the crime scenes…

01:33:20.540 --> 01:33:24.410
In order to mislead the police into thinking that the serial murders had ended at three.

01:33:25.740 --> 01:33:29.530
You ensured Kabe Souko-san was severely injured…

01:33:30.310 --> 01:33:34.870
Because you were afraid she would notice the irregular note, since she has perfect pitch.

01:33:35.410 --> 01:33:38.000
Someone who fears those with perfect pitch…

01:33:38.380 --> 01:33:40.280
Must be one with perfect pitch himself.

01:33:41.400 --> 01:33:44.340
From that point alone, the culprit had to be you, Fuwa-san.

01:33:47.190 --> 01:33:48.310
There is another.

01:33:49.160 --> 01:33:51.670
Akiba Reiko-san also has perfect pitch.

01:34:00.100 --> 01:34:03.930
But, as your late son's fiancée…

01:34:04.860 --> 01:34:10.020
You couldn't bear to treat her as you did Souko-san, using life-threatening explosives.

01:34:13.090 --> 01:34:16.140
Therefore, you chose to put irritants in her drink…

01:34:16.700 --> 01:34:19.210
And attacked her using a truck and an air rifle.

01:34:19.660 --> 01:34:22.030
In order to prevent her from taking the stage…

01:34:22.680 --> 01:34:24.040
You wanted her unable to speak…

01:34:24.500 --> 01:34:26.970
Or at least have her leg broken, right?

01:35:08.250 --> 01:35:09.140
That chord…

01:35:13.360 --> 01:35:14.180
The note!

01:35:27.810 --> 01:35:28.570
Why?

01:35:29.110 --> 01:35:29.820
Why didn't…

01:35:30.280 --> 01:35:31.640
It won't explode.

01:35:32.910 --> 01:35:34.830
Before I came here…

01:35:34.830 --> 01:35:38.010
I removed the sensor from the pipe.

01:35:38.420 --> 01:35:39.210
Three minutes.

01:35:39.730 --> 01:35:41.460
No, it took me two minutes.

01:35:45.850 --> 01:35:47.280
That's remarkable, little boy.

01:35:47.690 --> 01:35:49.300
What was your name again?

01:35:50.380 --> 01:35:52.770
Edogawa Conan, detective.

01:35:56.230 --> 01:35:57.330
Bravo!

01:35:57.580 --> 01:35:59.090
Bravo!

01:35:59.380 --> 01:36:01.650
Bravo, bravo!

01:36:04.730 --> 01:36:05.230
There he is.

01:36:05.700 --> 01:36:06.810
He's holding a remote control.

01:36:07.470 --> 01:36:08.940
Then it really was him…

01:36:09.750 --> 01:36:10.600
What should we do?

01:36:11.300 --> 01:36:13.190
Rush in before he sets off the bomb?

01:36:13.190 --> 01:36:13.830
That won't work!

01:36:14.470 --> 01:36:17.210
If we rush in, he'll set the bomb off by remote control.

01:36:18.040 --> 01:36:19.440
Then, what can we do?

01:36:21.760 --> 01:36:22.670
That room…

01:36:23.430 --> 01:36:25.700
We might be able to do something from that room.

01:36:25.950 --> 01:36:26.840
Something?

01:36:27.960 --> 01:36:28.890
Shoot him.

01:36:29.380 --> 01:36:31.230
Before he presses the remote control.

01:36:37.270 --> 01:36:38.870
Unfortunately, little detective…

01:36:39.760 --> 01:36:42.230
This remote control can also set off the explosion.

01:36:42.790 --> 01:36:44.190
You have lost.

01:36:44.390 --> 01:36:45.200
I wonder.

01:36:45.710 --> 01:36:47.110
We still don't know that yet.

01:36:49.380 --> 01:36:50.810
What don't we know?

01:36:51.860 --> 01:36:54.830
Even though I don't know how you got into the concert hall…

01:36:55.620 --> 01:36:58.380
Seeing as how the police haven't raided the place yet…

01:36:58.860 --> 01:37:03.460
The hall is probably engulfed in a sea of flames and inaccessible, just as I planned.

01:37:05.230 --> 01:37:07.830
The removal of the sensor was a miscalculation on my part, but…

01:37:09.360 --> 01:37:10.260
No matter.

01:37:10.730 --> 01:37:14.210
At least now I will be able to choose the moment of the explosion.

01:37:16.410 --> 01:37:17.840
As a parting gift…

01:37:18.400 --> 01:37:21.020
I'll send you to heaven while you're performing…

01:37:27.690 --> 01:37:28.980
Damn, at that time…

01:37:30.280 --> 01:37:34.320
Just as you perform on your precious organ…

01:37:35.400 --> 01:37:36.700
Doumoto Kazuki!

01:37:46.510 --> 01:37:47.280
Conan-kun!?

01:37:48.030 --> 01:37:49.040
It's no use.

01:37:49.040 --> 01:37:50.170
I can't fire like this.

01:38:00.470 --> 01:38:01.470
That's it.

01:38:01.470 --> 01:38:04.310
Hurry and begin your performance, Doumoto.

01:38:04.560 --> 01:38:05.220
What should I do?

01:38:05.800 --> 01:38:07.730
If I can't use my stun-gun wristwatch…

01:38:08.450 --> 01:38:09.690
What else can I do?

01:38:12.630 --> 01:38:13.660
Move aside, Conan-kun…

01:38:14.620 --> 01:38:15.400
Please!

01:38:24.190 --> 01:38:24.840
Give me that!

01:38:24.840 --> 01:38:26.080
My recorder!

01:38:26.900 --> 01:38:27.670
My voice is back!

01:38:31.160 --> 01:38:32.670
Yes, just like that…

01:38:33.040 --> 01:38:33.590
This is bad!

01:38:42.710 --> 01:38:44.310
Farewell, little detective.

01:38:44.740 --> 01:38:45.440
Like I'd let you!

01:38:52.440 --> 01:38:55.270
Mi-La-La-La-Fa?

01:38:57.030 --> 01:38:57.760
''SHOOT''?

01:38:57.950 --> 01:38:58.530
Someone's shooting?

01:38:59.490 --> 01:39:00.450
What was that sound?

01:39:01.040 --> 01:39:02.990
It's the sound that signals the end of the game.

01:39:03.490 --> 01:39:03.910
What?

01:39:16.780 --> 01:39:17.700
This is the police!

01:39:17.700 --> 01:39:18.180
Don't move!

01:39:20.420 --> 01:39:21.770
I have lost.

01:39:23.260 --> 01:39:31.260
♪ Chaconne in G Minor
Tomaso Antonio Vitali

01:40:14.530 --> 01:40:15.220
Fuwa-san…

01:40:15.650 --> 01:40:16.730
Where are the remaining bombs?

01:40:17.200 --> 01:40:19.700
Inside the ceiling above the stage.

01:40:20.480 --> 01:40:22.520
Takagi-kun, contact the inspector.

01:40:22.760 --> 01:40:23.300
Yes!

01:40:24.370 --> 01:40:25.720
I'm sorry, but…

01:40:26.500 --> 01:40:30.040
Would you allow me to listen to the rest of the performance?

01:40:30.560 --> 01:40:33.220
I'll tell you everything afterward.

01:40:44.790 --> 01:40:45.520
Understood.

01:40:46.010 --> 01:40:48.280
The fire on this side has finally been put out.

01:40:48.630 --> 01:40:49.630
We'll be there shortly.

01:40:49.630 --> 01:40:50.290
Inspector!

01:40:51.660 --> 01:40:53.400
There's an opening on the east side.

01:40:54.020 --> 01:40:54.790
All right, let's go.

01:40:55.530 --> 01:40:56.460
I'll get back to you.

01:41:02.440 --> 01:41:03.160
Say…

01:41:03.740 --> 01:41:06.200
Why did you plant bombs in this hall?

01:41:07.660 --> 01:41:10.350
For the last 35 years, I was his…

01:41:11.480 --> 01:41:14.130
I was Doumoto Kazuki's exclusive piano tuner…

01:41:14.550 --> 01:41:16.500
We had walked through life together.

01:41:19.840 --> 01:41:21.210
And then, two years ago…

01:41:21.560 --> 01:41:24.380
He suddenly retired from being a pianist.

01:41:28.540 --> 01:41:29.550
And then he told me…

01:41:30.050 --> 01:41:34.610
That he hoped I would become the director of Doumoto Hall, which was to be completed in two years time.

01:41:35.190 --> 01:41:37.700
Of course, I could have refused.

01:41:38.360 --> 01:41:41.780
I was free to continue as a piano tuner.

01:41:42.300 --> 01:41:50.230
But, after being the sole piano tuner of the internationally renowned pianist Doumoto Kazuki for the last 35 years…

01:41:50.660 --> 01:41:54.330
I couldn't permit myself to accept another pianist after so long.

01:41:54.890 --> 01:41:57.200
My pride wouldn't allow it.

01:41:57.900 --> 01:42:00.990
Even having said that, I am just a mechanic.

01:42:01.380 --> 01:42:03.930
I couldn't believe I was suited to the work of a director.

01:42:04.430 --> 01:42:07.260
I fell into despair.

01:42:45.260 --> 01:42:48.310
Two years ago, my wife passed away due to an illness.

01:42:48.890 --> 01:42:51.760
A year after that, my son died in an accident.

01:42:52.330 --> 01:42:58.190
In addition, after losing my job as a piano- tuner, the only meaningful thing in my life…

01:42:58.750 --> 01:43:01.650
I was left with nothing.

01:43:02.650 --> 01:43:05.110
Even the music which I once loved so much…

01:43:05.640 --> 01:43:09.620
Had become nothing but dissonant sounds that hurt me to listen to.

01:43:13.670 --> 01:43:14.520
Right…

01:43:14.900 --> 01:43:16.620
Even in my dreams, I could hear them…

01:43:17.160 --> 01:43:20.210
They would give me nightmares, and one night I decided…

01:43:21.090 --> 01:43:22.590
I would erase them…

01:43:23.000 --> 01:43:24.660
I would erase everything…

01:43:25.840 --> 01:43:28.630
In order to retake the silent night!

01:43:29.220 --> 01:43:32.100
Of course, the four who stole my son's life…

01:43:32.100 --> 01:43:33.570
The ever-selfish Doumoto…

01:43:33.570 --> 01:43:37.480
Whose interest in the piano was snatched away by the pipe organ and Doumoto Hall…

01:43:37.970 --> 01:43:41.680
And even those people who had come to hear the organ…

01:43:42.030 --> 01:43:45.940
The lives of the musicians and audience members from all over the world.

01:43:46.840 --> 01:43:52.020
I accepted the offer to become the director of Doumoto Hall…

01:43:52.020 --> 01:43:53.490
To gain access to the organ.

01:43:54.300 --> 01:43:56.650
To carry out my plan to plant the bombs here in the hall…

01:43:56.650 --> 01:43:59.670
It was best for me to go ahead and become the director.

01:44:00.080 --> 01:44:04.850
On the other hand, the piano which was abandoned together with me…

01:44:04.850 --> 01:44:06.400
I couldn't help but pity it.

01:44:07.050 --> 01:44:07.880
That means…

01:44:08.560 --> 01:44:11.550
Blowing up the piano alongside the practice room…

01:44:11.550 --> 01:44:13.830
Was your way of showing your love for the piano, huh?

01:44:14.680 --> 01:44:17.580
That's all I have to say.

01:44:18.280 --> 01:44:19.060
And now…

01:44:22.770 --> 01:44:24.730
Call Doumoto here right now.

01:44:25.210 --> 01:44:26.780
Fuwa-san, calm down!

01:44:27.260 --> 01:44:28.190
Don't be alarmed.

01:44:28.570 --> 01:44:30.050
This is for me to commit suicide.

01:44:30.470 --> 01:44:32.520
I have no intention of hurting anyone.

01:44:33.350 --> 01:44:35.740
Conan-kun, please leave the room.

01:44:35.940 --> 01:44:36.620
Forget it!

01:44:36.880 --> 01:44:38.310
Despite your numerous dreadful deeds…

01:44:38.570 --> 01:44:40.460
For you to die before atoning for them…

01:44:40.810 --> 01:44:42.380
I won't let you to do something so unfair!

01:44:42.380 --> 01:44:43.390
Conan-kun!

01:44:43.570 --> 01:44:45.590
Fuwa-san, please don't do anything foolish!

01:44:45.910 --> 01:44:46.890
Shut up!

01:44:46.890 --> 01:44:48.230
Call Doumoto here right now!

01:44:48.650 --> 01:44:49.350
Fuwa-kun.

01:44:51.400 --> 01:44:53.100
I'm right here.

01:44:55.960 --> 01:44:56.810
Doumoto-san!

01:45:01.060 --> 01:45:02.950
Fuwa-kun, I'm truly sorry.

01:45:03.340 --> 01:45:06.480
I failed to think you would brood so much over it.

01:45:06.890 --> 01:45:08.090
You've finally realized?

01:45:08.440 --> 01:45:10.680
Due to your selfishness, I was so—

01:45:10.680 --> 01:45:12.410
It wasn't like that, Fuwa-kun.

01:45:12.850 --> 01:45:15.750
The reason I retired from being a pianist was…

01:45:15.750 --> 01:45:20.040
Because I realized that your tuning had started to fail slightly.

01:45:21.750 --> 01:45:23.630
I considered your pride…

01:45:23.630 --> 01:45:25.600
And couldn't bear to make it known to you.

01:45:26.370 --> 01:45:30.670
Having said that, even now, I still cannot work with another tuner.

01:45:31.520 --> 01:45:34.360
So, I retired from the piano.

01:45:34.360 --> 01:45:35.390
Nonsense!

01:45:35.390 --> 01:45:37.190
I have perfect pitch!

01:45:37.190 --> 01:45:40.350
Indeed, you have perfect pitch.

01:45:40.660 --> 01:45:44.270
But with age, your hearing has deteriorated, hasn't it?

01:45:44.920 --> 01:45:49.790
There were times when you let the sound go out of tune without realizing it yourself.

01:45:52.570 --> 01:45:55.800
Lies! Lies! Lies! All lies!

01:45:56.410 --> 01:46:01.390
If I had known that this would happened, I would have told you the truth back then.

01:46:01.740 --> 01:46:03.880
I'm very sorry.

01:46:03.880 --> 01:46:05.400
It's too late to apologize now!

01:46:05.400 --> 01:46:06.970
It's all your fault!

01:46:06.970 --> 01:46:07.740
That's not true.

01:46:09.480 --> 01:46:12.960
If my close friend did something like that to me…

01:46:13.500 --> 01:46:16.930
I would wonder whether she had some unavoidable reason…

01:46:17.810 --> 01:46:24.890
And whether, perhaps, it might have been done in consideration of my own situation more than for my friend's personal benefit.

01:46:25.460 --> 01:46:27.150
That's what I would think.

01:46:28.080 --> 01:46:29.110
That's because…

01:46:30.460 --> 01:46:32.450
I trust that friend.

01:46:34.230 --> 01:46:35.610
It's the same for me.

01:47:04.590 --> 01:47:07.100
To think that all these explosions happened outside…

01:47:07.440 --> 01:47:09.380
I didn't notice anything at all.

01:47:10.110 --> 01:47:12.780
It seems Conan-kun really played an active role too.

01:47:13.280 --> 01:47:16.530
I knew it! It's just as I said, isn't it?

01:47:17.150 --> 01:47:22.030
At any rate, I'm surprised that Shinichi actually understood the recorder code…

01:47:22.650 --> 01:47:24.960
Replacing the notes with letters from the alphabet…

01:47:25.300 --> 01:47:27.370
It's something that happens in detective novels too.

01:47:27.810 --> 01:47:30.670
Even though in German notation, the note 'C' means 'H'…

01:47:31.450 --> 01:47:35.390
He knows that my mother is British.

01:47:35.740 --> 01:47:39.770
So 'C' becomes 'B', because he knows that I used the British names for the notes.

01:47:40.150 --> 01:47:42.100
I figured he would deduce that instantly.

01:47:42.760 --> 01:47:46.570
Besides, I was counting on his perfect pitch.

01:47:46.570 --> 01:47:47.770
Oh, I see.

01:47:48.770 --> 01:47:51.400
Moreover, I also believe in him…

01:47:52.480 --> 01:47:53.730
As his partner.

01:47:56.370 --> 01:48:00.200
And I was so sure that the Beethoven guy was our culprit…

01:48:00.450 --> 01:48:02.390
Dad, you're still saying that?

01:48:03.000 --> 01:48:06.070
But, you know, he never did show up in the end.

01:48:06.070 --> 01:48:07.310
That deduction moron.

01:48:07.630 --> 01:48:08.890
Oh, Shinichi?

01:48:09.260 --> 01:48:10.890
I can't be bothered with that guy.

01:48:11.510 --> 01:48:12.710
Let's go, Conan-kun.

01:48:13.500 --> 01:48:14.220
Huh?

01:48:14.220 --> 01:48:15.880
He was here just a moment ago.

01:48:19.030 --> 01:48:19.560
Huh?

01:48:25.180 --> 01:48:25.710
Hey…

01:48:26.000 --> 01:48:26.810
This sound…

01:48:30.170 --> 01:48:31.060
A violin.

01:48:31.600 --> 01:48:33.190
''Amazing Grace'', right?

01:48:33.540 --> 01:48:35.740
Not that. This playing style…

01:48:36.050 --> 01:48:36.690
Playing style?

01:48:39.210 --> 01:48:40.120
Shinichi?

01:48:41.810 --> 01:48:42.490
Wait, Ran!

01:48:59.440 --> 01:49:00.410
Shinichi!

01:49:01.410 --> 01:49:02.530
Shinichi!

01:49:04.250 --> 01:49:06.220
Shinichi-niichan already left.

01:49:07.770 --> 01:49:08.510
Conan-kun!

01:49:08.890 --> 01:49:09.850
He said he had a case.

01:49:10.670 --> 01:49:12.390
Shinichi really came then?

01:49:12.650 --> 01:49:13.280
Yeah.

01:49:14.310 --> 01:49:16.180
After hearing Reiko-san's song…

01:49:16.180 --> 01:49:18.150
He remembered what happened three years ago…

01:49:18.650 --> 01:49:23.570
And he used this violin from the school to play the piece just now…

01:49:24.180 --> 01:49:28.220
So that he and Ran-neechan could hear it together…

01:49:30.510 --> 01:49:34.180
Shinichi-niichan said he did something bad to you.

01:49:35.370 --> 01:49:36.570
Did you have a fight or something?

01:49:38.320 --> 01:49:39.470
It was nothing.

01:49:41.530 --> 01:49:43.970
I would have forgiven you even if you hadn't come…

01:49:48.630 --> 01:49:50.260
Idiot.

